WEBVTT

00:02:42.512 --> 00:02:45.242
<i>The hills are alive</i>

00:02:45.549 --> 00:02:49.918
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:02:50.187 --> 00:02:52.621
<i>With songs they have sung</i>

00:02:52.923 --> 00:02:57.758
<i>For a thousand years</i>

00:02:58.028 --> 00:03:01.191
<i>The hills fill my heart</i>

00:03:01.431 --> 00:03:05.959
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:03:06.236 --> 00:03:13.404
<i>My heart wants to sing</i>
<i>Every song it hears</i>

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:18.779
<i>My heart wants to beat like the wings</i>
<i>Of the birds that rise</i>

00:03:19.049 --> 00:03:22.109
<i>From the lake to the trees</i>

00:03:22.319 --> 00:03:26.619
<i>My heart wants to sigh</i>
<i>Like a chime that flies</i>

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:30.826
<i>From a church on a breeze</i>

00:03:31.094 --> 00:03:34.586
<i>To laugh like a brook</i>
<i>When it trips and falls</i>

00:03:34.831 --> 00:03:38.323
<i>Over stones on its way</i>

00:03:38.602 --> 00:03:42.470
<i>To sing through the night</i>

00:03:42.739 --> 00:03:46.505
<i>Like a lark who is learning to pray</i>

00:03:46.843 --> 00:03:52.475
<i>I go to the hills</i>

00:03:52.682 --> 00:03:58.848
<i>When my heart is lonely</i>

00:03:59.122 --> 00:04:02.990
<i>I know I will hear</i>

00:04:03.193 --> 00:04:07.687
<i>What I've heard before</i>

00:04:07.964 --> 00:04:12.697
<i>My heart will be blessed</i>

00:04:12.936 --> 00:04:20.707
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:04:21.778 --> 00:04:26.943
<i>And I'll sing...</i>

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:36.115
<i>...once more</i>

00:09:18.174 --> 00:09:23.134
<i>Hallelujah, hallelujah</i>

00:09:23.413 --> 00:09:28.077
<i>Hallelujah, hallelujah</i>

00:09:30.286 --> 00:09:32.345
- Reverend Mother.
- Sister Bernice.

00:09:32.589 --> 00:09:35.217
- I simply cannot find her.
- Maria?

00:09:36.292 --> 00:09:37.589
She's missing again.

00:09:38.528 --> 00:09:40.894
We should've put a cowbell
around her neck.

00:09:41.131 --> 00:09:44.191
Have you tried the barn? You know
how much she adores the animals.

00:09:44.467 --> 00:09:47.197
I have looked everywhere.
In all of the usual places.

00:09:47.403 --> 00:09:49.633
Sister, considering it's Maria...

00:09:49.939 --> 00:09:52.533
...I suggest you look in someplace
unusual.

00:09:57.814 --> 00:09:59.111
Well, Reverend Mother...

00:09:59.382 --> 00:10:01.942
...I hope this new infraction ends
whatever doubts...

00:10:02.218 --> 00:10:05.449
...you may still have
about Maria's future here.

00:10:05.655 --> 00:10:09.716
I always try to keep faith
in my doubts, Sister Berthe.

00:10:09.959 --> 00:10:12.826
After all, the wool of a black sheep
is just as warm.

00:10:13.062 --> 00:10:17.396
We are not talking about sheep,
black or white, Sister Margaretta.

00:10:17.634 --> 00:10:21.070
Of all the candidates for
the novitiate, Maria is the least...

00:10:21.337 --> 00:10:23.828
Children, children.

00:10:24.307 --> 00:10:28.266
We were speculating about
the qualifications of our postulants.

00:10:28.912 --> 00:10:31.904
The Mistress of Novices
and the Mistress of Postulants...

00:10:32.148 --> 00:10:37.450
...were trying to help me
by expressing opposite points of view.

00:10:37.687 --> 00:10:40.747
Tell me, Sister Catherine,
what do you think of Maria?

00:10:40.957 --> 00:10:44.017
She's a wonderful girl,
some of the time.

00:10:44.994 --> 00:10:48.088
- Sister Agatha?
- It's very easy to like Maria...

00:10:48.331 --> 00:10:50.856
...except when it's difficult.

00:10:51.167 --> 00:10:54.728
- And you, Sister Sophia?
- Oh, I love her very dearly.

00:10:54.938 --> 00:10:57.873
But she always seems to be
in trouble, doesn't she?

00:10:58.107 --> 00:10:59.699
Exactly what I say.

00:11:00.176 --> 00:11:02.644
<i>She climbs a tree and scrapes her knee</i>

00:11:02.846 --> 00:11:04.541
<i>Her dress has got a tear</i>

00:11:05.215 --> 00:11:09.379
<i>She waltzes on her way to Mass</i>
<i>And whistles on the stair</i>

00:11:10.019 --> 00:11:14.513
<i>And underneath her wimple</i>
<i>She has curlers in her hair</i>

00:11:14.791 --> 00:11:19.387
<i>I've even heard her singing</i>
<i>In the abbey</i>

00:11:19.629 --> 00:11:21.620
<i>She's always late for chapel</i>

00:11:21.865 --> 00:11:24.129
<i>But her penitence is real</i>

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:26.732
<i>She's always late for everything</i>

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:28.995
<i>Except for every meal</i>

00:11:29.372 --> 00:11:34.071
<i>I hate to have to say it</i>
<i>But I very firmly feel</i>

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:38.747
<i>Maria's not an asset to the abbey</i>

00:11:39.249 --> 00:11:41.740
<i>I'd like to say a word in her behalf</i>

00:11:42.018 --> 00:11:43.349
Say it, Sister Margaretta.

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:48.179
<i>Maria makes me laugh</i>

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:54.996
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:11:55.265 --> 00:11:59.065
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

00:11:59.369 --> 00:12:02.702
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

00:12:03.239 --> 00:12:04.331
<i>A flibbertigibbet</i>

00:12:04.574 --> 00:12:05.905
<i>- A will-o'-the-wisp</i>
<i>- A clown</i>

00:12:07.543 --> 00:12:11.274
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

00:12:11.547 --> 00:12:15.005
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

00:12:15.418 --> 00:12:19.115
<i>But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>And listen to all you say?</i>

00:12:19.689 --> 00:12:23.181
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

00:12:23.426 --> 00:12:27.522
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:12:28.031 --> 00:12:33.560
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam...</i>

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:39.231
<i>...in your hand?</i>

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:43.802
<i>When I'm with her I'm confused</i>
<i>Out of focus and bemused</i>

00:12:44.113 --> 00:12:47.549
<i>And I never know exactly where I am</i>

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:51.083
<i>- Unpredictable as weather</i>
<i>- She's as flighty as a feather</i>

00:12:51.454 --> 00:12:53.285
<i>- She's a darling</i>
<i>- She's a demon</i>

00:12:53.489 --> 00:12:54.820
<i>She's a lamb</i>

00:12:55.224 --> 00:12:58.887
<i>She'll out pester any pest</i>
<i>Drive a hornet from its nest</i>

00:12:59.095 --> 00:13:02.394
<i>She can throw a whirling dervish</i>
<i>Out of whirl</i>

00:13:02.966 --> 00:13:06.493
<i>- She is gentle, she is wild</i>
<i>- She's a riddle, she's a child</i>

00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:09.630
<i>- She's a headache</i>
<i>- She's an angel</i>

00:13:09.839 --> 00:13:13.741
<i>She's a girl</i>

00:13:14.477 --> 00:13:18.413
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:13:18.648 --> 00:13:22.345
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

00:13:22.652 --> 00:13:26.144
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

00:13:26.422 --> 00:13:28.413
<i>- A flibbertigibbet</i>
<i>- A will-o'-the-wisp</i>

00:13:28.658 --> 00:13:30.285
<i>A clown</i>

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:34.491
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

00:13:34.764 --> 00:13:38.256
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

00:13:38.468 --> 00:13:42.802
<i>- But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>- And listen to all you say?</i>

00:13:43.039 --> 00:13:47.135
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

00:13:47.343 --> 00:13:53.179
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:14:09.132 --> 00:14:15.901
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam...</i>

00:14:16.806 --> 00:14:23.211
<i>...in your hand?</i>

00:14:35.024 --> 00:14:37.015
You may go in now, Maria.

00:14:49.605 --> 00:14:51.232
Come here, my child.

00:14:57.747 --> 00:14:59.112
Now sit down.

00:15:00.049 --> 00:15:03.610
Reverend Mother, I'm sorry.
I couldn't help myself.

00:15:03.886 --> 00:15:06.855
- The hills were beckoning and before...
- Dear.

00:15:07.256 --> 00:15:09.224
I haven't summoned you for apologies.

00:15:09.459 --> 00:15:11.689
Please let me ask for forgiveness.

00:15:12.361 --> 00:15:13.589
If you'll feel better.

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:16.896
Yes, you see,
the sky was so blue today...

00:15:17.133 --> 00:15:20.933
...and everything was so green and
fragrant, I had to be a part of it.

00:15:21.204 --> 00:15:25.698
The Untersberg led me higher like
it wanted me to go through the clouds.

00:15:25.908 --> 00:15:27.933
Suppose darkness had come
and you were lost?

00:15:28.211 --> 00:15:30.441
Mother, I could never be lost
up there.

00:15:30.713 --> 00:15:33.546
That's my mountain.
I was brought up on it.

00:15:33.749 --> 00:15:36.047
It was the mountain that led me
to you.

00:15:36.819 --> 00:15:39.788
When I was a child,
I would come down and climb a tree...

00:15:40.056 --> 00:15:41.819
...and look in your garden.

00:15:42.058 --> 00:15:44.993
I'd see the sisters at work
and hear them sing.

00:15:46.329 --> 00:15:49.958
Which brings me to another
transgression, Reverend Mother.

00:15:50.166 --> 00:15:52.327
I was singing out there today.

00:15:53.002 --> 00:15:57.029
Only in the abbey do we have rules
about postulants singing.

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:59.265
I can't stop wherever I am.

00:15:59.475 --> 00:16:01.807
Worse, I can't seem to stop
saying things.

00:16:02.078 --> 00:16:04.342
Everything I think and feel.

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:06.013
Some call that "honesty."

00:16:06.282 --> 00:16:08.648
Oh, but it's terrible,
Reverend Mother!

00:16:08.851 --> 00:16:12.753
You know how Sister Berthe makes me
kiss the floor after a disagreement?

00:16:13.122 --> 00:16:16.614
Lately, I kiss the floor
when I see her coming to save time.

00:16:19.295 --> 00:16:20.455
Maria...

00:16:21.464 --> 00:16:24.456
...when you saw us over the wall
and longed to be with us...

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:29.433
...that didn't mean you were prepared
for the way we live here, did it?

00:16:30.773 --> 00:16:33.173
No, Mother, but I pray and I try.

00:16:33.376 --> 00:16:35.105
And I am learning. I really am.

00:16:35.344 --> 00:16:38.006
What is the most important lesson
you have learned here?

00:16:38.681 --> 00:16:42.481
To find out what is the will of God
and do it wholeheartedly.

00:16:45.321 --> 00:16:46.447
Maria...

00:16:47.957 --> 00:16:50.721
...it seems to be God's will
that you leave us.

00:16:50.993 --> 00:16:52.483
- Leave?
- Only for a while.

00:16:52.995 --> 00:16:55.327
No, Mother!
Please don't send me away!

00:16:55.565 --> 00:16:59.831
This is where I belong. It's my home,
my family. It's my life.

00:17:00.503 --> 00:17:03.529
- Are you truly ready for it?
- Yes, I am.

00:17:03.739 --> 00:17:08.642
If you go out into the world for a
time, knowing what we expect of you...

00:17:08.911 --> 00:17:11.641
...you will find out
if you can expect it of yourself.

00:17:11.847 --> 00:17:16.147
I know what you expect, Mother,
and I can do it! I promise I can!

00:17:19.689 --> 00:17:20.917
Yes, Mother.

00:17:23.025 --> 00:17:24.686
If it is God's will.

00:17:26.929 --> 00:17:32.060
There is a family near Salzburg that
needs a governess until September.

00:17:32.268 --> 00:17:34.498
- September?
- For seven children.

00:17:35.171 --> 00:17:36.160
Seven children?!

00:17:36.405 --> 00:17:37.667
Do you like children?

00:17:38.441 --> 00:17:40.272
Well, yes, but seven!

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.573
I will tell Captain von Trapp
to expect you tomorrow.

00:17:45.114 --> 00:17:46.513
Captain?

00:17:47.216 --> 00:17:52.051
A retired officer of the Imperial
Navy. A fine man and a brave one.

00:17:52.288 --> 00:17:55.018
His wife died,
and he is alone with the children.

00:17:55.224 --> 00:17:59.524
I understand he has had a difficult
time keeping a governess there.

00:18:00.296 --> 00:18:02.594
Why difficult, Reverend Mother?

00:18:03.966 --> 00:18:06.901
The Lord will show you
in His own good time.

00:18:43.773 --> 00:18:46.241
When the Lord closes a door...

00:18:46.442 --> 00:18:48.967
...somewhere He opens a window.

00:18:51.314 --> 00:18:56.308
<i>What will this day be like?</i>

00:18:56.519 --> 00:18:58.749
<i>I wonder</i>

00:19:05.261 --> 00:19:09.357
<i>What will my future be?</i>

00:19:10.199 --> 00:19:12.463
<i>I wonder</i>

00:19:14.036 --> 00:19:17.130
<i>It could be so exciting</i>

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:20.434
<i>To be out in the world</i>
<i>To be free</i>

00:19:20.643 --> 00:19:23.703
<i>My heart should be wildly rejoicing</i>

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:30.216
<i>Oh, what's the matter with me?</i>

00:19:30.553 --> 00:19:33.613
<i>I've always longed for adventure</i>

00:19:33.889 --> 00:19:37.450
<i>To do the things I've never dared</i>

00:19:37.693 --> 00:19:40.890
<i>Now here I'm facing adventure</i>

00:19:41.197 --> 00:19:47.295
<i>Then why am I so scared?</i>

00:19:50.740 --> 00:19:53.641
<i>A captain with seven children</i>

00:19:53.876 --> 00:19:56.709
<i>What's so fearsome about that?</i>

00:19:59.248 --> 00:20:01.876
<i>I must stop these doubts and worries</i>

00:20:02.151 --> 00:20:04.984
<i>If I don't I just know I'll turn back</i>

00:20:05.254 --> 00:20:08.417
<i>I must dream of the things</i>
<i>I am seeking</i>

00:20:09.492 --> 00:20:14.486
<i>I am seeking the courage I lack</i>

00:20:15.398 --> 00:20:19.232
<i>The courage to serve them</i>
<i>With reliance</i>

00:20:19.502 --> 00:20:22.403
<i>Face my mistakes without defiance</i>

00:20:22.671 --> 00:20:24.366
<i>Show them I'm worthy</i>

00:20:24.607 --> 00:20:27.269
<i>And while I show them</i>

00:20:27.543 --> 00:20:31.343
<i>I'll show me</i>

00:20:31.547 --> 00:20:36.951
<i>So let them bring on</i>
<i>All their problems</i>

00:20:37.186 --> 00:20:40.451
<i>I'll do better than my best</i>

00:20:40.723 --> 00:20:43.783
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>They'll put me to the test</i>

00:20:44.026 --> 00:20:47.462
<i>But I'll make them see</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:20:47.696 --> 00:20:50.961
<i>Somehow I will impress them</i>

00:20:51.233 --> 00:20:54.464
<i>I will be firm but kind</i>

00:20:54.737 --> 00:20:58.036
<i>And all those children</i>
<i>Heaven bless them</i>

00:20:58.274 --> 00:21:01.573
<i>They will look up to me</i>
<i>And mind me</i>

00:21:01.811 --> 00:21:04.939
<i>With each step I am more certain</i>

00:21:05.214 --> 00:21:08.479
<i>Everything will turn out fine</i>

00:21:08.717 --> 00:21:11.811
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>The world can all be mine</i>

00:21:12.054 --> 00:21:17.492
<i>They'll have to agree</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:21:19.061 --> 00:21:21.791
<i>I have confidence in sunshine</i>

00:21:22.064 --> 00:21:25.158
<i>I have confidence in rain</i>

00:21:25.401 --> 00:21:28.268
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>That spring will come again</i>

00:21:28.571 --> 00:21:31.597
<i>Besides which you see</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:21:31.907 --> 00:21:34.967
<i>Strength doesn't lie in numbers</i>

00:21:35.244 --> 00:21:38.270
<i>Strength doesn't lie in wealth</i>

00:21:38.514 --> 00:21:41.847
<i>Strength lies in nights</i>
<i>Of peaceful slumbers</i>

00:21:42.117 --> 00:21:44.984
<i>When you wake up, wake up</i>
<i>It's healthy</i>

00:21:45.287 --> 00:21:48.279
<i>All I trust I leave my heart to</i>

00:21:48.524 --> 00:21:51.425
<i>All I trust becomes my own</i>

00:21:51.627 --> 00:21:56.428
<i>I have confidence in confidence alone</i>

00:22:11.046 --> 00:22:12.673
Oh, help.

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:31.527
<i>I have confidence in confidence alone</i>

00:22:32.334 --> 00:22:37.135
<i>Besides which you see</i>
<i>I have confidence...</i>

00:22:37.406 --> 00:22:44.209
<i>...in me</i>

00:22:50.753 --> 00:22:53.153
Hello. Here I am.

00:22:55.991 --> 00:22:57.822
I'm from the convent.
I'm the new governess, captain.

00:22:59.495 --> 00:23:02.726
And I'm the old butler, fräulein.

00:23:04.700 --> 00:23:06.497
Well, how do you do?

00:23:17.012 --> 00:23:21.073
You'll wait here, please.

00:24:47.436 --> 00:24:51.532
In future, remember certain rooms
in this house are not to be disturbed.

00:24:52.708 --> 00:24:54.175
Yes, captain, sir.

00:25:02.117 --> 00:25:07.350
- Why do you stare at me that way?
- You don't look like a sea captain.

00:25:08.557 --> 00:25:11.617
I'm afraid you don't look
very much like a governess.

00:25:12.327 --> 00:25:13.385
- Turn around.
- What?

00:25:13.729 --> 00:25:14.991
Turn.

00:25:18.167 --> 00:25:19.327
Hat off.

00:25:22.538 --> 00:25:25.166
Put on another dress
before meeting the children.

00:25:25.474 --> 00:25:27.032
But I don't have another.

00:25:27.309 --> 00:25:30.176
When we enter the abbey,
our worldly clothes go to the poor.

00:25:30.412 --> 00:25:31.674
What about this one?

00:25:31.880 --> 00:25:33.211
The poor didn't want it.

00:25:35.050 --> 00:25:38.542
There wasn't time to make a new dress.
I can make clothes.

00:25:39.822 --> 00:25:42.086
I'll see that you get some material.

00:25:42.825 --> 00:25:44.349
Today, if possible.

00:25:45.327 --> 00:25:47.090
- Now, fräulein...
- Maria.

00:25:47.329 --> 00:25:50.059
I don't know how much
the abbess told you.

00:25:50.332 --> 00:25:52.892
You are the twelfth governess...

00:25:53.102 --> 00:25:55.570
...to look after my children
since their mother died.

00:25:55.771 --> 00:25:58.001
I trust you will be an improvement
on the last one.

00:25:58.240 --> 00:26:00.071
She stayed only two hours.

00:26:01.777 --> 00:26:04.371
What's wrong with the children, sir?

00:26:05.848 --> 00:26:10.251
Nothing is wrong with the children,
only the governesses.

00:26:10.519 --> 00:26:15.456
They could not maintain discipline,
without which the house cannot be run.

00:26:16.391 --> 00:26:18.188
Drill them in their studies.

00:26:18.427 --> 00:26:21.919
I will not permit them to dream
away their summer holidays.

00:26:22.197 --> 00:26:24.893
Each afternoon,
they march, breathing deeply.

00:26:25.100 --> 00:26:26.761
Bedtime is to be strictly observed.

00:26:26.969 --> 00:26:27.936
When do they play?

00:26:28.137 --> 00:26:32.198
You will see to it that they conduct
themselves with the utmost decorum.

00:26:32.441 --> 00:26:35.376
- I am placing you in command.
- Yes, sir.

00:27:56.024 --> 00:27:57.184
Now...

00:27:57.793 --> 00:28:00.728
...this is your new governess,
Fräulein Maria.

00:28:02.397 --> 00:28:04.388
Give your name at your signal.

00:28:04.700 --> 00:28:08.898
Fräulein, listen carefully. Learn
their signals so you can call them.

00:28:10.205 --> 00:28:11.570
Liesl.

00:28:11.840 --> 00:28:13.569
Friedrich.

00:28:13.842 --> 00:28:15.366
Louisa.

00:28:15.644 --> 00:28:16.906
Kurt.

00:28:17.145 --> 00:28:18.203
Brigitta.

00:28:18.480 --> 00:28:19.708
Marta.

00:28:26.088 --> 00:28:27.419
Gretl.

00:28:32.060 --> 00:28:35.496
Now, let's see how well you listened.

00:28:35.731 --> 00:28:38.097
I won't need to whistle for them,
Reverend Captain.

00:28:38.367 --> 00:28:41.825
I mean, I'll use their names.
Such lovely names.

00:28:42.037 --> 00:28:45.200
Fräulein, this is a large house.
The grounds are extensive.

00:28:45.440 --> 00:28:48.204
And I will not have anyone shouting.

00:28:48.443 --> 00:28:50.172
You will take this, please.
Learn to use it.

00:28:50.379 --> 00:28:52.040
The children will help you.

00:28:54.082 --> 00:28:58.075
Now, when I want you,
this is what you will hear.

00:28:58.954 --> 00:29:00.751
Oh, no, sir. I'm sorry, sir!

00:29:01.623 --> 00:29:03.181
I could never answer to a whistle.

00:29:03.392 --> 00:29:06.020
Whistles are for animals,
not for children.

00:29:06.295 --> 00:29:08.354
And definitely not for me.

00:29:08.597 --> 00:29:11.225
It would be too humiliating.

00:29:12.034 --> 00:29:17.233
Fräulein, were you this much trouble
at the abbey?

00:29:17.539 --> 00:29:18.631
Oh, much more, sir.

00:29:29.751 --> 00:29:31.309
I don't know your signal.

00:29:32.788 --> 00:29:35.416
You may call me "captain."

00:29:48.337 --> 00:29:49.804
At ease.

00:29:52.607 --> 00:29:54.165
Now that there's just us...

00:29:54.443 --> 00:29:58.607
...would you please tell me all your
names again and how old you are.

00:29:59.081 --> 00:30:03.074
I'm Liesl. I'm 16 years old,
and I don't need a governess.

00:30:03.852 --> 00:30:06.912
I'm glad you told me, Liesl.
We'll just be good friends.

00:30:09.091 --> 00:30:12.857
I'm Friedrich. I'm 14.
I'm impossible.

00:30:13.161 --> 00:30:14.822
Really? Who told you that, Friedrich?

00:30:15.097 --> 00:30:18.589
Fräulein Josephine.
Four governesses ago.

00:30:19.034 --> 00:30:20.501
I'm Brigitta.

00:30:22.337 --> 00:30:26.330
You didn't tell me how old you are,
Louisa.

00:30:27.009 --> 00:30:29.273
I'm Brigitta. She's Louisa.

00:30:29.511 --> 00:30:32.275
She's 13 years old, and you're smart.

00:30:32.514 --> 00:30:36.280
I'm 10, and I think your dress
is the ugliest one I ever saw.

00:30:36.618 --> 00:30:39.246
- Brigitta, you shouldn't say that.
- Why not?

00:30:39.454 --> 00:30:41.718
- Don't you think it's ugly?
- Of course.

00:30:41.990 --> 00:30:44.686
But Fräulein Helga's was ugliest.

00:30:44.960 --> 00:30:47.554
I'm Kurt. I'm 11.
I'm incorrigible.

00:30:47.829 --> 00:30:50.957
- Congratulations.
- What's "incorrigible"?

00:30:51.199 --> 00:30:55.067
I think it means you want
to be treated like a boy.

00:30:57.239 --> 00:31:00.538
I'm Marta, and I'm going to be
seven on Tuesday.

00:31:00.809 --> 00:31:02.174
I'd like a pink parasol.

00:31:03.378 --> 00:31:04.902
Pink's my favorite color too.

00:31:07.315 --> 00:31:08.475
Yes, you're Gretl.

00:31:09.384 --> 00:31:11.079
And you're five years old?

00:31:11.520 --> 00:31:13.511
My, you're practically a lady.

00:31:16.024 --> 00:31:19.050
I have to tell you a secret.
I've never been a governess.

00:31:20.495 --> 00:31:23.259
You don't know anything
about being a governess?

00:31:23.532 --> 00:31:24.897
Nothing. I'll need lots of advice.

00:31:25.867 --> 00:31:30.395
The best way to start is to tell
Father to mind his own business.

00:31:30.605 --> 00:31:32.402
Never come to dinner on time.

00:31:32.607 --> 00:31:34.905
Never eat your soup quietly.

00:31:35.577 --> 00:31:37.670
During dessert, always blow your nose.

00:31:37.913 --> 00:31:40.711
Don't you believe a word they say,
Fräulein Maria.

00:31:40.916 --> 00:31:44.283
- Oh, why not?
- Because I like you.

00:31:45.087 --> 00:31:47.078
Children, outside for your walk.

00:31:47.289 --> 00:31:49.189
Father's orders. Hurry up.

00:31:49.391 --> 00:31:50.688
Quick, quick, quick.

00:31:50.926 --> 00:31:54.123
Fräulein Maria, I'm Frau Schmidt,
the housekeeper.

00:31:54.362 --> 00:31:55.420
How do you do.

00:31:55.630 --> 00:31:58.531
I'll show you to your room.
Follow me.

00:32:09.611 --> 00:32:11.374
Poor little dears.

00:32:24.092 --> 00:32:28.461
You're very lucky. With
Fräulein Helga it was a snake.

00:32:42.310 --> 00:32:43.641
Good evening.

00:32:45.080 --> 00:32:48.641
- Good evening, children.
- Good evening, Fräulein Maria.

00:32:55.857 --> 00:32:57.484
Enchanting little ritual.

00:32:57.692 --> 00:33:00.422
Something you learned at the abbey?

00:33:01.630 --> 00:33:03.962
No.

00:33:05.600 --> 00:33:06.862
Rheumatism.

00:33:16.678 --> 00:33:19.841
Excuse me, captain. Haven't we
forgotten to thank the Lord?

00:33:28.056 --> 00:33:31.025
For what we receive,
may the Lord make us truly thankful.

00:33:31.560 --> 00:33:33.494
- Amen.
- Amen.

00:33:38.033 --> 00:33:39.967
I'd like to thank you all...

00:33:40.168 --> 00:33:43.160
...for the precious gift
you left in my pocket today.

00:33:46.675 --> 00:33:48.472
What gift?

00:33:51.580 --> 00:33:53.741
It's a secret between
the children and me.

00:33:54.015 --> 00:33:57.644
Then I suggest you keep it,
and let us eat.

00:33:58.019 --> 00:33:59.987
Knowing how nervous
I must have been...

00:34:00.222 --> 00:34:02.656
...a stranger in a new household...

00:34:02.857 --> 00:34:05.917
...knowing how important it was
for me to feel accepted...

00:34:06.194 --> 00:34:10.392
...it was so kind and thoughtful of
you to make my first moments here...

00:34:10.665 --> 00:34:12.860
...so warm and happy...

00:34:13.068 --> 00:34:14.831
...and pleasant.

00:34:24.079 --> 00:34:26.104
- What is the matter, Marta?
- Nothing.

00:34:38.526 --> 00:34:39.550
Fräulein...

00:34:39.794 --> 00:34:43.628
...is it to be at every meal
or merely at dinnertime...

00:34:43.865 --> 00:34:48.427
...that you intend leading us through
this rare and wonderful new world...

00:34:48.637 --> 00:34:50.298
...of indigestion?

00:34:51.873 --> 00:34:54.740
They're all right, captain.
They're just happy.

00:35:13.495 --> 00:35:16.157
- Rolfe, good evening.
- Good evening, Franz.

00:35:16.431 --> 00:35:19.161
- I trust everything is under control?
- Yes, yes.

00:35:20.802 --> 00:35:23.236
- Are there any developments?
- Perhaps.

00:35:23.438 --> 00:35:25.599
- Is the captain home?
- He's at dinner.

00:35:25.840 --> 00:35:28.172
- With the family?
- Yes.

00:35:28.443 --> 00:35:30.240
Give him this telegram at once.

00:35:30.979 --> 00:35:32.071
Certainly.

00:35:43.758 --> 00:35:45.453
A telegram for you, sir.

00:35:48.296 --> 00:35:50.127
Franz? Who delivered it?

00:35:50.432 --> 00:35:52.457
That young lad Rolfe, of course.

00:35:54.803 --> 00:35:56.532
Father, may I be excused?

00:35:57.505 --> 00:36:01.965
Children, in the morning I shall
be going to Vienna.

00:36:02.277 --> 00:36:04.711
Not again, Father!

00:36:08.616 --> 00:36:10.675
How long will you be gone this time?

00:36:11.319 --> 00:36:12.786
I'm not sure, Gretl.

00:36:12.987 --> 00:36:16.548
- To visit Baroness Schraeder again?
- Mind your own business!

00:36:17.525 --> 00:36:19.459
As a matter of fact, yes, Louisa.

00:36:21.229 --> 00:36:25.063
- Why can't we ever see the baroness?
- Why would she want to see you?

00:36:25.367 --> 00:36:30.236
You are going to see the baroness.
I'm bringing her back with me to visit.

00:36:31.740 --> 00:36:33.537
And Uncle Max.

00:36:33.808 --> 00:36:36.208
Uncle Max!

00:36:52.260 --> 00:36:53.591
Rolfe!

00:36:56.664 --> 00:36:57.722
Oh, Rolfe!

00:37:00.268 --> 00:37:03.203
- No, Liesl. We mustn't!
- Why not, silly?

00:37:03.438 --> 00:37:06.100
- I don't know...
- Isn't this why you're waiting?

00:37:06.341 --> 00:37:08.206
Yes, of course.

00:37:08.410 --> 00:37:11.208
- I've missed you, Liesl.
- You have? How much?

00:37:11.446 --> 00:37:15.280
I even thought of sending a telegram,
so I'd be able to deliver it here.

00:37:15.550 --> 00:37:19.452
Oh, that's a lovely thought!
Why don't you, right now?

00:37:19.721 --> 00:37:23.885
- But I'm here!
- Please, Rolfe. Send me a telegram.

00:37:24.092 --> 00:37:27.550
I'll start it for you.
"Dear Liesl..."

00:37:28.229 --> 00:37:31.858
"Dear Liesl: I'd like to be able
to tell you...

00:37:32.100 --> 00:37:34.295
...how I feel about you. Stop.

00:37:34.536 --> 00:37:39.064
Unfortunately, this wire
is already too expensive.

00:37:39.274 --> 00:37:40.707
Sincerely, Rolfe."

00:37:40.909 --> 00:37:43.673
- "Sincerely"?
- Cordially.

00:37:43.878 --> 00:37:46.540
- "Cordially"?
- Affectionately?

00:37:48.917 --> 00:37:50.942
Will there be any reply?

00:37:52.220 --> 00:37:54.381
"Dear Rolfe: Stop.

00:37:55.390 --> 00:37:58.484
Don't stop! Your Liesl."

00:38:00.228 --> 00:38:04.062
If only we didn't have to wait
for someone to send Father a telegram.

00:38:04.332 --> 00:38:06.732
How do I know when I'll see you again?

00:38:07.635 --> 00:38:08.829
Well, let's see...

00:38:11.840 --> 00:38:13.808
I could come here by mistake.

00:38:14.809 --> 00:38:19.439
With a telegram for Colonel Schneider!
He's here from Berlin staying with...

00:38:20.348 --> 00:38:23.647
No one knows he's here.
Don't tell your father.

00:38:23.918 --> 00:38:27.081
- Why not?
- Your father's so Austrian.

00:38:27.288 --> 00:38:28.585
We're all Austrian.

00:38:28.790 --> 00:38:33.193
Some think we ought to be German, and
they're very mad at those who don't.

00:38:33.428 --> 00:38:35.191
They're getting ready to...

00:38:36.865 --> 00:38:39.299
Let's hope your father
doesn't get into trouble.

00:38:39.601 --> 00:38:44.504
Don't worry. He's a big naval hero.
He was even decorated by the emperor.

00:38:44.706 --> 00:38:47.971
I don't worry about him.
I worry about his daughter.

00:38:48.510 --> 00:38:49.977
Me? Why?

00:38:50.278 --> 00:38:51.836
- Well, you're so...
- What?

00:38:52.280 --> 00:38:53.770
You're such a baby!

00:38:54.215 --> 00:38:57.116
I'm 16.
What's such a baby about that?

00:38:59.354 --> 00:39:02.881
<i>You wait, little girl</i>
<i>On an empty stage</i>

00:39:03.124 --> 00:39:06.491
<i>For fate to turn the light on</i>

00:39:07.128 --> 00:39:10.359
<i>Your life, little girl</i>
<i>Is an empty page</i>

00:39:10.632 --> 00:39:14.693
<i>That men will want to write on</i>

00:39:15.403 --> 00:39:20.898
<i>To write on</i>

00:39:21.843 --> 00:39:25.779
<i>You are 16 going on 17</i>

00:39:25.980 --> 00:39:29.814
<i>Baby, it's time to think</i>

00:39:30.018 --> 00:39:33.647
<i>Better beware</i>
<i>Be canny and careful</i>

00:39:33.888 --> 00:39:37.517
<i>Baby, you're on the brink</i>

00:39:37.859 --> 00:39:41.693
<i>You are 16 going on 17</i>

00:39:41.896 --> 00:39:45.559
<i>Fellows will fall in line</i>

00:39:45.867 --> 00:39:49.200
<i>Eager young lads</i>
<i>And roués and cads</i>

00:39:49.404 --> 00:39:53.340
<i>Will offer you food and wine</i>

00:39:53.608 --> 00:39:57.374
<i>Totally unprepared are you</i>

00:39:57.779 --> 00:40:01.340
<i>To face a world of men</i>

00:40:01.916 --> 00:40:06.080
<i>Timid and shy and scared are you</i>

00:40:06.387 --> 00:40:09.879
<i>Of things beyond your ken</i>

00:40:10.091 --> 00:40:13.959
<i>You need someone older and wiser</i>

00:40:14.195 --> 00:40:18.063
<i>Telling you what to do</i>

00:40:18.299 --> 00:40:21.735
<i>I am 17 going on 18</i>

00:40:21.970 --> 00:40:27.931
<i>I'll take care of you</i>

00:41:00.475 --> 00:41:03.808
<i>I am 16 going on 17</i>

00:41:04.012 --> 00:41:07.413
<i>I know that I'm naive</i>

00:41:07.682 --> 00:41:10.913
<i>Fellows I meet</i>
<i>May tell me I'm sweet</i>

00:41:11.152 --> 00:41:14.849
<i>And willingly I believe</i>

00:41:15.323 --> 00:41:18.486
<i>I am 16 going on 17</i>

00:41:18.693 --> 00:41:22.459
<i>Innocent as a rose</i>

00:41:22.664 --> 00:41:26.122
<i>Bachelor dandies</i>
<i>Drinkers of brandies</i>

00:41:26.434 --> 00:41:29.767
<i>What do I know of those?</i>

00:41:29.971 --> 00:41:33.498
<i>Totally unprepared am I</i>

00:41:33.775 --> 00:41:37.267
<i>To face a world of men</i>

00:41:37.679 --> 00:41:41.012
<i>Timid and shy and scared am I</i>

00:41:41.282 --> 00:41:44.945
<i>Of things beyond my ken</i>

00:41:45.386 --> 00:41:48.981
<i>I need someone older and wiser</i>

00:41:49.223 --> 00:41:52.522
<i>Telling me what to do</i>

00:41:52.860 --> 00:41:56.557
<i>You are 17 going on 18</i>

00:41:56.798 --> 00:42:02.464
<i>I'll depend on you</i>

00:43:55.516 --> 00:43:56.949
Come in.

00:43:57.985 --> 00:43:59.612
Frau Schmidt.

00:44:01.956 --> 00:44:03.685
For your new dresses.

00:44:03.991 --> 00:44:07.984
- The captain had these sent from town.
- Oh, how lovely!

00:44:08.262 --> 00:44:11.698
These will make the prettiest
clothes I've ever had.

00:44:11.966 --> 00:44:15.458
Do you think he would
get me more material if I asked?

00:44:15.703 --> 00:44:19.332
- How many dresses do you need?
- Not for me, for the children.

00:44:19.607 --> 00:44:21.666
I want to make them some play clothes.

00:44:21.943 --> 00:44:25.470
The von Trapp children don't play.
They march.

00:44:25.980 --> 00:44:28.380
Surely you don't approve of that.

00:44:29.383 --> 00:44:31.783
Ever since the captain
lost his poor wife...

00:44:32.019 --> 00:44:34.715
...he runs this house as if on
one of his ships.

00:44:35.556 --> 00:44:36.955
Whistles, orders.

00:44:37.225 --> 00:44:39.056
No more music, no more laughing.

00:44:39.327 --> 00:44:42.854
Nothing that reminds him of her.
Even the children.

00:44:43.364 --> 00:44:44.456
But that's so wrong.

00:44:45.299 --> 00:44:46.823
Oh, well.

00:44:47.034 --> 00:44:50.697
How do you like your room?
There'll be new drapes at the windows.

00:44:50.972 --> 00:44:52.234
Bu these are fine.

00:44:52.473 --> 00:44:54.134
New ones have been ordered.

00:44:54.342 --> 00:44:57.641
- But I really don't need them.
- Good night, now.

00:44:57.879 --> 00:45:01.906
Frau Schmidt, if I asked
the captain about the material...?

00:45:02.183 --> 00:45:06.643
- He's leaving in the morning.
- Of course. How long will he be gone?

00:45:07.221 --> 00:45:11.817
It depends. The last time he visited
the baroness, he stayed for a month.

00:45:12.994 --> 00:45:17.556
I shouldn't be saying this to you.
I don't know you that well.

00:45:17.832 --> 00:45:20.733
But if you ask me,
the captain's thinking seriously...

00:45:20.935 --> 00:45:23.233
...of marrying her before
summer's over.

00:45:23.437 --> 00:45:26.668
Wonderful! The children will
have a mother again.

00:45:28.109 --> 00:45:29.406
Yes.

00:45:29.677 --> 00:45:31.406
Well, good night.

00:45:31.612 --> 00:45:33.045
Good night.

00:45:51.465 --> 00:45:54.298
Dear Father, now I know
why You sent me here.

00:45:54.535 --> 00:45:57.402
To help these children
prepare for a new mother.

00:45:57.638 --> 00:46:00.937
And I pray this will become
a happy family in Thy sight.

00:46:01.142 --> 00:46:04.270
God bless the captain.
God bless Liesl and Friedrich.

00:46:04.478 --> 00:46:08.642
God bless Louisa, Brigitta,
Marta and little Gretl.

00:46:08.950 --> 00:46:11.783
And I forgot the other boy.
What's his name?

00:46:13.554 --> 00:46:15.385
Well, God bless what's-his-name.

00:46:15.589 --> 00:46:19.582
God bless the Reverend Mother
and Sister Margaretta...

00:46:19.794 --> 00:46:21.591
...and everybody at the abbey.

00:46:21.796 --> 00:46:24.321
And now, dear God, about Liesl.

00:46:24.832 --> 00:46:26.732
Help her know that I'm her friend...

00:46:26.934 --> 00:46:29.494
...and help her tell me
what she's been up to.

00:46:30.237 --> 00:46:31.397
Are you going to tell on me?

00:46:31.639 --> 00:46:35.075
Help me to be understanding
so I may guide her footsteps.

00:46:35.343 --> 00:46:37.971
In the name of the Father,
the Son and the Holy Ghost.

00:46:38.179 --> 00:46:41.171
I was out walking
and somebody locked the doors early.

00:46:41.482 --> 00:46:45.111
I didn't want to wake everybody,
so when I saw your window open...

00:46:46.754 --> 00:46:49.780
You're not going to tell Father,
are you?

00:46:55.863 --> 00:46:57.160
How did you climb up?

00:46:57.665 --> 00:47:00.793
It's how we always got in
to play tricks on the governess.

00:47:01.002 --> 00:47:03.994
Louisa can make it with
a whole jar of spiders in her hand.

00:47:05.006 --> 00:47:06.667
Spiders?

00:47:10.378 --> 00:47:13.006
Were you out walking all by yourself?

00:47:20.488 --> 00:47:24.185
If we wash that dress tonight,
nobody would notice it tomorrow.

00:47:24.859 --> 00:47:26.622
You could put this on.

00:47:28.362 --> 00:47:31.058
Take your dress and put it
to soak in the bathtub.

00:47:31.298 --> 00:47:34.825
Come back here and sit on the bed,
and we'll have a talk.

00:47:36.137 --> 00:47:39.163
I told you today
I didn't need a governess.

00:47:39.373 --> 00:47:41.466
Well, maybe I do.

00:48:11.939 --> 00:48:14.499
Gretl, are you scared?

00:48:18.012 --> 00:48:20.276
You're not frightened
of a storm, are you?

00:48:20.514 --> 00:48:22.778
You just stay right here with me.

00:48:23.951 --> 00:48:28.183
- Where are the others?
- They're asleep. They're not scared.

00:48:32.593 --> 00:48:34.424
Oh, no? Look.

00:48:35.963 --> 00:48:37.931
All right, up here on the bed.

00:48:38.232 --> 00:48:40.928
- Really?
- Well, just this once. Come on.

00:48:42.036 --> 00:48:46.370
- Now we'll wait for the boys.
- You won't see them. Boys are brave.

00:48:52.446 --> 00:48:54.243
You weren't scared, were you?

00:48:54.782 --> 00:48:57.979
Oh, no. We just wanted
to be sure that you weren't.

00:48:59.086 --> 00:49:02.112
- That's very thoughtful of you.
- It wasn't my idea.

00:49:02.423 --> 00:49:04.254
It was Kurt's!

00:49:04.492 --> 00:49:07.086
Kurt! That's the one I left out!
God bless Kurt.

00:49:09.897 --> 00:49:11.660
Why does it do that?

00:49:11.899 --> 00:49:15.733
The lightning talks to the thunder,
and the thunder answers.

00:49:15.970 --> 00:49:18.461
- But lightning must be nasty.
- Not really.

00:49:18.739 --> 00:49:21.003
Why does the thunder get so angry?

00:49:21.275 --> 00:49:23.402
It makes me want to cry.

00:49:25.279 --> 00:49:29.477
Whenever I'm feeling unhappy,
I just try to think of nice things.

00:49:29.683 --> 00:49:31.514
What kind of things?

00:49:32.286 --> 00:49:34.254
Well, let me see. Nice things...

00:49:34.488 --> 00:49:35.580
Daffodils.

00:49:36.857 --> 00:49:38.256
Green meadows.

00:49:38.659 --> 00:49:40.923
Skies full of stars.

00:49:41.128 --> 00:49:44.325
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>
<i>and whiskers on kittens</i>

00:49:44.532 --> 00:49:47.660
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

00:49:47.868 --> 00:49:51.031
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

00:49:51.305 --> 00:49:55.298
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:49:57.878 --> 00:50:00.676
<i>Cream-colored ponies</i>
<i>And crisp apple strudels</i>

00:50:00.948 --> 00:50:04.145
<i>Doorbells and sleigh bells</i>
<i>And schnitzel with noodles</i>

00:50:04.385 --> 00:50:07.320
<i>Wild geese that fly</i>
<i>With the moon on their wings</i>

00:50:07.555 --> 00:50:11.389
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:50:12.660 --> 00:50:15.390
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:50:15.663 --> 00:50:18.860
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

00:50:19.133 --> 00:50:22.193
<i>Silver white winters</i>
<i>That melt into springs</i>

00:50:22.469 --> 00:50:25.836
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:50:26.040 --> 00:50:27.735
<i>When the dog bites</i>

00:50:27.975 --> 00:50:29.636
<i>When the bee stings</i>

00:50:29.877 --> 00:50:32.141
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

00:50:32.379 --> 00:50:35.746
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

00:50:36.016 --> 00:50:42.854
<i>And then I don't feel so bad</i>

00:50:43.591 --> 00:50:45.252
- Does it work?
- Of course.

00:50:45.559 --> 00:50:47.493
- What do you like?
- Pussy willow!

00:50:48.195 --> 00:50:50.425
- Christmas!
- Bunny rabbits!

00:50:50.664 --> 00:50:52.325
Snakes!

00:50:52.600 --> 00:50:54.727
- Chocolate icing!
- No school!

00:50:55.035 --> 00:50:56.161
Pillow fights!

00:50:56.437 --> 00:50:58.428
- Telegrams!
- Birthday presents!

00:50:58.839 --> 00:51:01.205
- Any presents!
- Ladybugs!

00:51:02.710 --> 00:51:04.041
A good sneeze!

00:51:04.345 --> 00:51:06.074
Gesundheit!

00:51:06.380 --> 00:51:07.608
See what fun it is?

00:51:07.848 --> 00:51:10.783
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>
<i>And whiskers on kittens</i>

00:51:11.051 --> 00:51:13.918
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

00:51:14.188 --> 00:51:17.180
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

00:51:17.424 --> 00:51:20.257
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:23.697 --> 00:51:26.530
<i>Cream-colored ponies</i>
<i>And crisp apple strudels</i>

00:51:26.767 --> 00:51:29.634
<i>Doorbells and sleigh bells</i>
<i>And schnitzel with noodles</i>

00:51:29.870 --> 00:51:32.805
<i>Wild geese that fly</i>
<i>With the moon on their wings</i>

00:51:33.073 --> 00:51:36.565
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:37.544 --> 00:51:39.034
Together.

00:51:39.313 --> 00:51:42.077
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:51:42.316 --> 00:51:45.217
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

00:51:45.452 --> 00:51:48.444
<i>Silver white winters</i>
<i>That melt into springs</i>

00:51:48.722 --> 00:51:51.987
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:52.293 --> 00:51:54.420
<i>When the dog bi...</i>

00:51:54.628 --> 00:51:56.596
Dog bites.

00:52:03.237 --> 00:52:04.465
Hello.

00:52:04.672 --> 00:52:08.836
Fräulein, did I not tell you that
bedtime is to be strictly observed?

00:52:09.143 --> 00:52:11.839
The children were upset
by the storm, so l...

00:52:13.247 --> 00:52:14.236
You did, sir.

00:52:14.448 --> 00:52:18.646
Do you, or do you not, have difficulty
remembering such simple instructions?

00:52:19.953 --> 00:52:21.580
Only during thunderstorms.

00:52:24.091 --> 00:52:25.581
Liesl?

00:52:25.826 --> 00:52:28.021
I don't recall seeing you
after dinner.

00:52:28.629 --> 00:52:30.358
Really? As a matter of fact...

00:52:30.631 --> 00:52:31.859
Yes?

00:52:32.666 --> 00:52:33.826
Well, I was...

00:52:34.101 --> 00:52:36.160
What she would like to say...

00:52:36.370 --> 00:52:39.271
...is that she and I have
been getting acquainted tonight.

00:52:39.473 --> 00:52:44.342
It's too late to go into that. You
heard your father. Go back to bed.

00:52:48.982 --> 00:52:50.381
Fräulein...

00:52:50.684 --> 00:52:54.711
...you have managed to remember
I'm leaving in the morning?

00:52:55.823 --> 00:53:00.351
Is it also possible you remember the
first rule in this house is discipline?

00:53:02.029 --> 00:53:04.520
Then I trust that before I return...

00:53:05.032 --> 00:53:06.795
...you'll have acquired some?

00:53:08.168 --> 00:53:09.533
Captain?

00:53:10.504 --> 00:53:14.406
Could I talk to you about clothes
for the children for when they play?

00:53:14.675 --> 00:53:17.371
- If I could have some material.
- You are many things.

00:53:17.644 --> 00:53:19.805
Not the least of which is repetitious.

00:53:20.013 --> 00:53:22.174
- But they're children!
- Yes.

00:53:22.416 --> 00:53:24.179
And I'm their father.

00:53:24.752 --> 00:53:25.980
Good night.

00:53:50.244 --> 00:53:56.080
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:54:07.594 --> 00:54:11.121
<i>When the dog bites</i>
<i>When the bee stings</i>

00:54:11.365 --> 00:54:13.856
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

00:54:14.101 --> 00:54:17.400
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

00:54:17.604 --> 00:54:19.731
<i>And then I don't feel...</i>

00:54:19.973 --> 00:54:26.902
<i>...so bad</i>

00:54:50.904 --> 00:54:53.600
Children, over here. See!

00:54:57.244 --> 00:54:58.609
Come on.

00:56:21.662 --> 00:56:22.890
Fräulein Maria?

00:56:23.163 --> 00:56:25.063
Can we do this every day?

00:56:25.365 --> 00:56:28.562
- Don't you think you'd get tired of it?
- I suppose so.

00:56:28.902 --> 00:56:30.164
Every other day?

00:56:30.370 --> 00:56:35.000
I haven't had so much fun since we put
glue on Fräulein Josephine's toothbrush.

00:56:35.208 --> 00:56:39.110
I can't understand how children
as nice as you can play such tricks.

00:56:39.379 --> 00:56:41.210
- It's easy.
- But why do it?

00:56:41.415 --> 00:56:43.849
How else can we get
Father's attention?

00:56:44.618 --> 00:56:46.210
Oh, I see.

00:56:47.554 --> 00:56:49.749
We'll have to think about that one.

00:56:51.925 --> 00:56:53.552
All right, over here.

00:56:53.760 --> 00:56:55.193
What are we going to do?

00:56:55.429 --> 00:56:57.397
Think of a song for the baroness.

00:56:57.631 --> 00:56:59.599
Father doesn't like us to sing.

00:56:59.866 --> 00:57:03.427
Perhaps we can change his mind.
Now, what songs do you know?

00:57:03.704 --> 00:57:05.865
We don't know any songs.

00:57:06.106 --> 00:57:08.768
- Not any?
- We don't even know how to sing.

00:57:10.444 --> 00:57:12.605
Let's not lose time. You must learn.

00:57:12.879 --> 00:57:14.608
But how?

00:57:18.919 --> 00:57:22.878
<i>Let's start at the very beginning</i>

00:57:23.090 --> 00:57:26.457
<i>A very good place to start</i>

00:57:26.660 --> 00:57:28.594
<i>When you read you begin with</i>

00:57:28.829 --> 00:57:30.057
<i>A, B, C</i>

00:57:30.263 --> 00:57:34.597
<i>When you sing, you begin with</i>
<i>Do-Re-Mi</i>

00:57:34.835 --> 00:57:36.462
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:36.737 --> 00:57:38.068
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:38.305 --> 00:57:42.139
<i>The first three notes</i>
<i>Just happen to be</i>

00:57:42.409 --> 00:57:44.172
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:44.411 --> 00:57:45.673
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:45.912 --> 00:57:49.848
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti</i>

00:57:50.517 --> 00:57:52.951
Let's see if I can make it easier.

00:57:56.356 --> 00:58:00.019
<i>"Doe," a deer</i>
<i>A female deer</i>

00:58:00.260 --> 00:58:03.821
<i>"Ray," a drop of golden sun</i>

00:58:04.097 --> 00:58:07.863
<i>"Me," a name I call myself</i>

00:58:08.135 --> 00:58:11.832
<i>"Far," a long long way to run</i>

00:58:12.105 --> 00:58:15.871
<i>"Sew," a needle pulling thread</i>

00:58:16.176 --> 00:58:20.010
<i>"La," a note to follow sew</i>

00:58:20.280 --> 00:58:23.215
<i>"Tea," a drink with jam and bread</i>

00:58:23.684 --> 00:58:27.780
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

00:58:28.288 --> 00:58:31.849
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

00:58:32.125 --> 00:58:35.322
<i>- Ray</i>
<i>- A drop of golden sun</i>

00:58:35.562 --> 00:58:38.861
<i>- Me</i>
<i>- A name I call myself</i>

00:58:39.132 --> 00:58:42.226
<i>- Far</i>
<i>- A long long way to run</i>

00:58:42.736 --> 00:58:46.194
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

00:58:46.406 --> 00:58:49.739
<i>- La</i>
<i>- A note to follow sew</i>

00:58:50.177 --> 00:58:53.044
<i>- Tea</i>
<i>- A drink with jam and bread</i>

00:58:53.313 --> 00:58:55.577
<i>That will bring us back to</i>

00:58:55.816 --> 00:58:59.252
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

00:58:59.519 --> 00:59:02.579
<i>Ray, a drop of golden sun</i>

00:59:03.056 --> 00:59:06.253
<i>Me, a name I call myself</i>

00:59:06.526 --> 00:59:09.586
<i>Far, a long long way to run</i>

00:59:09.863 --> 00:59:13.094
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

00:59:13.400 --> 00:59:16.767
<i>La, a note to follow sew</i>

00:59:17.037 --> 00:59:19.665
<i>Tea, a drink with jam and bread</i>

00:59:19.873 --> 00:59:23.934
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

00:59:24.344 --> 00:59:27.438
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do, so-do</i>

00:59:27.881 --> 00:59:32.443
Do-re-mi-fa-so and so on are only
the tools we use to build a song.

00:59:32.719 --> 00:59:35.950
Once you have them in your head
you can sing different tunes...

00:59:36.223 --> 00:59:38.350
...by mixing them up. Like this:

00:59:39.593 --> 00:59:45.088
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

00:59:45.298 --> 00:59:46.390
Can you do that?

00:59:46.600 --> 00:59:52.095
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

00:59:52.305 --> 00:59:57.971
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

00:59:58.278 --> 01:00:03.580
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

01:00:03.784 --> 01:00:05.547
Now, put it all together.

01:00:05.752 --> 01:00:12.385
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

01:00:12.626 --> 01:00:18.587
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

01:00:19.166 --> 01:00:21.760
- Good.
- But it doesn't mean anything.

01:00:22.002 --> 01:00:24.971
So we put in words.
One word for every note.

01:00:25.238 --> 01:00:26.500
Like this:

01:00:26.740 --> 01:00:33.304
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:00:33.580 --> 01:00:39.177
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:00:39.452 --> 01:00:40.419
Together!

01:00:40.620 --> 01:00:47.321
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:00:47.527 --> 01:00:54.194
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:00:54.601 --> 01:00:57.968
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

01:00:58.238 --> 01:01:01.435
<i>- Ray</i>
<i>- A drop of golden sun</i>

01:01:01.708 --> 01:01:04.939
<i>- Me</i>
<i>- A name I call myself</i>

01:01:05.145 --> 01:01:08.205
<i>- Far</i>
<i>- A long long way to run</i>

01:01:08.448 --> 01:01:11.815
<i>- Sew</i>
<i>- A needle pulling thread</i>

01:01:12.118 --> 01:01:15.383
<i>- La</i>
<i>- A note to follow sew</i>

01:01:15.589 --> 01:01:18.581
<i>- Tea</i>
<i>- A drink with jam and bread</i>

01:01:18.792 --> 01:01:22.660
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

01:01:40.247 --> 01:01:46.516
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:01:47.087 --> 01:01:53.583
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:01:54.160 --> 01:01:57.323
<i>Doe</i>
<i>A deer, a female deer</i>

01:01:57.597 --> 01:02:01.124
<i>Ray</i>
<i>A drop of golden sun</i>

01:02:01.334 --> 01:02:04.792
<i>Me</i>
<i>A name I call myself</i>

01:02:05.038 --> 01:02:08.201
<i>Far</i>
<i>A long long way to run</i>

01:02:08.475 --> 01:02:11.638
<i>Sew</i>
<i>A needle pulling thread</i>

01:02:11.845 --> 01:02:15.042
<i>La</i>
<i>A note to follow sew</i>

01:02:15.649 --> 01:02:18.277
<i>Tea</i>
<i>A drink with jam and bread</i>

01:02:18.518 --> 01:02:22.477
<i>That will bring us back to</i>

01:02:22.689 --> 01:02:29.527
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

01:02:29.796 --> 01:02:34.290
<i>So-do-la-fa-ti</i>

01:02:34.534 --> 01:02:36.161
<i>La-so</i>

01:02:39.706 --> 01:02:45.508
<i>Ti-do</i>

01:02:45.712 --> 01:02:47.202
<i>So-do</i>

01:03:00.660 --> 01:03:03.754
The mountains are magnificent,
really magnificent.

01:03:03.997 --> 01:03:06.659
- I had them put up just for you.
- Oh?

01:03:06.933 --> 01:03:09.094
Even if it's to a height
of 10,000 feet...

01:03:09.369 --> 01:03:12.896
...Georg always believes in
"rising to the occasion."

01:03:13.173 --> 01:03:15.437
Improve the jokes
or I'll disinvite you.

01:03:16.042 --> 01:03:18.602
You didn't invite me.
I invited myself.

01:03:18.878 --> 01:03:21.403
- Naturally.
- You needed a chaperone...

01:03:21.681 --> 01:03:24.411
...and I needed a place
where the cuisine is superb...

01:03:24.684 --> 01:03:27.278
...the wine cellar unexcelled...

01:03:27.587 --> 01:03:30.181
...and the price perfect.

01:03:30.557 --> 01:03:32.388
Max, you are outrageous.

01:03:32.625 --> 01:03:36.618
Not at all.
I'm a very charming sponge.

01:03:39.265 --> 01:03:40.391
Listen.

01:03:42.736 --> 01:03:44.966
That's the Klopmann Monastery Choir.

01:03:47.974 --> 01:03:49.601
They're good.

01:03:50.643 --> 01:03:52.270
Very good.

01:03:53.079 --> 01:03:55.741
I must explore this area
in the next few days.

01:03:55.949 --> 01:03:59.407
Somewhere, a hungry singing group
is waiting for Max Detweiler...

01:03:59.652 --> 01:04:03.952
...to pluck it out and make it famous
at the Salzburg Folk Festival.

01:04:04.157 --> 01:04:07.456
- They get fame, you get money.
- It's unfair, I admit it.

01:04:07.727 --> 01:04:12.096
But someday that'll be changed.
I shall get the fame too.

01:04:19.139 --> 01:04:21.300
Good heavens, what's this?

01:04:22.742 --> 01:04:25.074
It's nothing.
Just some local urchins.

01:04:40.293 --> 01:04:44.195
This really is exciting for me, Georg.
Being here with you.

01:04:45.031 --> 01:04:47.591
Trees, lakes,
you've seen them before.

01:04:47.867 --> 01:04:50.461
That is not what I mean,
and you know it.

01:04:50.703 --> 01:04:54.662
- You mean me? I'm exciting?
- Is that so impossible?

01:04:54.941 --> 01:04:57.967
No, just highly improbable.

01:04:58.211 --> 01:05:02.375
- There you go, running yourself down.
- Well, I'm a dangerous driver.

01:05:06.152 --> 01:05:09.849
You're much less of a riddle
when I see you here, Georg.

01:05:10.056 --> 01:05:12.889
- In my natural habitat?
- Yes, exactly.

01:05:13.193 --> 01:05:15.320
Are you saying that I'm more
at home...

01:05:15.562 --> 01:05:19.555
...among the birds and the flowers
and the wind that moves...

01:05:19.833 --> 01:05:21.994
...through the trees
like a restless sea?

01:05:22.235 --> 01:05:23.827
How poetic.

01:05:24.037 --> 01:05:25.902
Yes, it was rather, wasn't it?

01:05:27.040 --> 01:05:32.171
More at home here than in Vienna
in all your glittering salons...

01:05:32.378 --> 01:05:36.747
...gossiping gaily with bores I
detest, soaking myself in champagne...

01:05:37.050 --> 01:05:40.747
...stumbling about to waltzes
by Strausses I can't even remember?

01:05:41.054 --> 01:05:43.181
- Is that what you're saying?
- Yes.

01:05:43.423 --> 01:05:45.721
Now whatever gave you that idea?

01:05:49.095 --> 01:05:52.997
Oh, I do like it here, Georg.
It's so lovely and peaceful.

01:05:53.333 --> 01:05:55.267
How can you leave it so often?

01:05:55.535 --> 01:05:58.368
Oh, pretending to be madly active,
I suppose.

01:05:58.605 --> 01:06:01.870
Activity suggests a life
filled with purpose.

01:06:02.609 --> 01:06:04.873
Could it be running away
from memories?

01:06:08.081 --> 01:06:12.017
Or perhaps just searching
for a reason to stay.

01:06:12.685 --> 01:06:16.177
I hope that's why you've been
coming to Vienna so often.

01:06:16.856 --> 01:06:21.190
- Were there other distractions?
- I'd hardly call you a distraction.

01:06:21.427 --> 01:06:24.089
Well, what would you call me, Georg?

01:06:26.366 --> 01:06:27.628
Lovely...

01:06:28.635 --> 01:06:31.263
...charming, witty, graceful,
the perfect hostess...

01:06:31.471 --> 01:06:34.304
...and, you're going to hate me
for this...

01:06:34.741 --> 01:06:36.800
...in a way, my savior.

01:06:37.076 --> 01:06:38.907
Oh, how unromantic.

01:06:39.112 --> 01:06:41.444
I'd be an ungrateful wretch
if I didn't say...

01:06:41.714 --> 01:06:44.945
...that you brought some meaning back
into my life.

01:06:46.786 --> 01:06:49.550
I am amusing, I suppose.

01:06:49.789 --> 01:06:54.556
I have the finest couturier in Vienna
and a glittering circle of friends.

01:06:54.761 --> 01:06:57.889
- I do give some rather gay parties.
- Oh, yes.

01:06:58.131 --> 01:06:59.962
But take all that away...

01:07:00.166 --> 01:07:04.603
...and you have just wealthy,
unattached little me...

01:07:05.271 --> 01:07:07.671
...searching, just like you.

01:07:12.779 --> 01:07:14.474
More strudel, Herr Detweiler?

01:07:14.747 --> 01:07:16.271
- How many have I had?
- Two.

01:07:16.516 --> 01:07:18.450
Make it an uneven three.

01:07:21.754 --> 01:07:24.780
Still eating, Max?
Must be unhappy.

01:07:24.991 --> 01:07:28.950
That mixed quartet I've been trying
to steal away from Sol Hurok...

01:07:29.195 --> 01:07:31.857
- What happened?
...Sascha Petrie stole them first.

01:07:32.098 --> 01:07:33.360
I hate thieves.

01:07:33.633 --> 01:07:36.932
Max, you really must try
and learn to love yourself.

01:07:37.170 --> 01:07:39.502
I had to call Paris, Rome
and Stockholm.

01:07:39.772 --> 01:07:43.333
- On Georg's telephone, of course.
- How else could I afford it?

01:07:43.810 --> 01:07:48.941
I like rich people, the way they live
and how I live when I'm with them.

01:07:49.282 --> 01:07:51.273
I wonder where the children are.

01:07:51.684 --> 01:07:54.175
They must have heard
I was coming and hid.

01:07:54.454 --> 01:07:56.945
I was hoping they'd be here
to welcome you.

01:07:57.190 --> 01:08:01.684
Max, do step out of character for
a moment and try and be charming.

01:08:10.737 --> 01:08:12.136
Well?

01:08:13.039 --> 01:08:14.233
Well what?

01:08:14.474 --> 01:08:17.375
Have you made up his mind?
Do I hear wedding bells?

01:08:17.644 --> 01:08:19.635
- Pealing madly.
- Marvelous.

01:08:19.879 --> 01:08:22.643
- Not necessarily for me.
- What kind of talk's that?

01:08:22.849 --> 01:08:24.407
None-of-your-business talk.

01:08:24.717 --> 01:08:27.151
I'm terribly fond of him,
so don't toy with us.

01:08:27.420 --> 01:08:31.015
But I'm a child. I like toys.
So tell me everything.

01:08:31.324 --> 01:08:36.387
Come on. Tell me every teensy-weensy,
intimate, disgusting detail.

01:08:37.864 --> 01:08:41.994
Well, let's just say I have a feeling
I may be here on approval.

01:08:42.235 --> 01:08:45.261
- I approve of that. How can you miss?
- Far too easily.

01:08:45.538 --> 01:08:48.769
If I know you, darling,
and I do, you will find a way.

01:08:49.042 --> 01:08:51.533
- He's no ordinary man.
- No, he's rich.

01:08:51.778 --> 01:08:54.042
His wife's death gave him
a great heartache.

01:08:54.247 --> 01:08:57.375
And your husband's death
gave you a great fortune.

01:08:57.583 --> 01:08:59.551
Oh, Max, you really are a beast.

01:08:59.752 --> 01:09:03.779
You and Georg are like family.
That's why I want to see you married.

01:09:04.023 --> 01:09:07.584
We must keep all that lovely money
in the family.

01:09:23.876 --> 01:09:26.811
- What are you doing there?
- Oh, Captain von Trapp.

01:09:27.080 --> 01:09:29.105
I was just looking for...

01:09:29.982 --> 01:09:32.815
I didn't see, I mean,
I didn't know you were...

01:09:33.419 --> 01:09:35.114
Heil Hitler!

01:09:35.822 --> 01:09:37.312
Who are you?

01:09:37.590 --> 01:09:39.820
I have a telegram for Herr Detweiler.

01:09:40.093 --> 01:09:42.823
- I am Herr Detweiler.
- Yes, sir.

01:09:47.900 --> 01:09:50.494
You've delivered your telegram.
Now get out.

01:09:57.276 --> 01:10:00.677
- Georg, he's just a boy.
- Yes, and I'm just an Austrian.

01:10:00.913 --> 01:10:03.677
Things will happen.
Make sure they don't happen to you.

01:10:03.983 --> 01:10:06.645
Max! Don't you ever say that again.

01:10:06.919 --> 01:10:09.114
I have no political convictions.

01:10:09.355 --> 01:10:12.290
- Can I help it if other people do?
- You can help it.

01:10:13.426 --> 01:10:15.587
You must help it.

01:10:25.872 --> 01:10:27.464
Hello?

01:10:30.109 --> 01:10:32.873
You're far away. Where are you?

01:10:33.179 --> 01:10:37.047
In a world that's disappearing,
I'm afraid.

01:10:37.884 --> 01:10:41.479
Is there any way I could bring you
back to the world I'm in?

01:11:07.413 --> 01:11:09.904
- Father! Father!
- There's your father!

01:11:10.716 --> 01:11:13.344
Oh, captain, you're home!

01:11:21.727 --> 01:11:24.389
Come out of that water at once!

01:11:33.506 --> 01:11:35.701
Oh, you must be Baroness Schraeder.

01:11:41.013 --> 01:11:44.005
I'm soaked to the skin!

01:11:55.962 --> 01:11:57.361
Straight line!

01:12:12.044 --> 01:12:14.444
This is Baroness Schraeder.

01:12:17.049 --> 01:12:18.812
And these...

01:12:19.051 --> 01:12:20.643
...are my children.

01:12:21.754 --> 01:12:23.244
How do you do?

01:12:24.323 --> 01:12:29.056
Go inside, dry off, clean up, change
your clothes and report back here!

01:12:34.066 --> 01:12:36.159
Fräulein, you will stay here, please!

01:12:37.904 --> 01:12:41.465
I think I'd better go see
what Max is up to.

01:12:51.684 --> 01:12:53.447
Now, fräulein...

01:12:55.354 --> 01:12:57.413
...I want a truthful answer.

01:12:57.823 --> 01:12:59.290
Yes, captain.

01:12:59.592 --> 01:13:03.653
Is it possible,
or could I have just imagined it?

01:13:05.164 --> 01:13:09.658
Have my children, by any chance,
been climbing trees today?

01:13:10.136 --> 01:13:11.296
Yes, captain.

01:13:12.371 --> 01:13:13.702
I see.

01:13:14.273 --> 01:13:18.767
And where, may I ask,
did they get these...

01:13:19.045 --> 01:13:21.104
- Play clothes.
- Is that what they are?

01:13:21.314 --> 01:13:24.715
I made them from the drapes
that used to hang in my bedroom.

01:13:25.518 --> 01:13:27.645
- Drapes?
- They have plenty of wear left.

01:13:27.853 --> 01:13:29.787
We've been everywhere in them.

01:13:30.022 --> 01:13:34.482
Are you telling me that my children
have been roaming about Salzburg...

01:13:34.694 --> 01:13:38.061
...dressed up in nothing
but some old drapes?

01:13:38.297 --> 01:13:39.958
And having a marvelous time!

01:13:40.166 --> 01:13:43.397
- They have uniforms.
- Forgive me, straitjackets.

01:13:43.636 --> 01:13:46.400
They can't be children
if they worry about clothes...

01:13:46.672 --> 01:13:47.798
They don't complain.

01:13:48.040 --> 01:13:50.736
They don't dare.
They love you too much and fear...

01:13:50.977 --> 01:13:52.535
Don't discuss my children.

01:13:52.745 --> 01:13:54.679
You've got to hear, you're
never home...

01:13:54.880 --> 01:13:56.404
I don't want to hear more!

01:13:56.649 --> 01:13:59.140
I know you don't, but you've got to!

01:13:59.919 --> 01:14:02.080
- Liesl's not a child.
- Not one word...

01:14:02.355 --> 01:14:05.222
Soon she'll be a woman
and you won't even know her.

01:14:05.491 --> 01:14:08.551
Friedrich wants to be a man
but you're not here to show...

01:14:08.828 --> 01:14:10.159
Don't you dare tell me...

01:14:10.396 --> 01:14:13.661
Brigitta could tell you about him.
She notices everything.

01:14:13.899 --> 01:14:17.027
Kurt acts tough to hide the pain
when you ignore him...

01:14:17.236 --> 01:14:18.760
...the way you do all of them.

01:14:19.038 --> 01:14:21.438
Louisa, I don't know about yet.

01:14:21.707 --> 01:14:24.904
The little ones just want love.
Please, love them all.

01:14:25.177 --> 01:14:26.701
I don't care to hear more.

01:14:26.946 --> 01:14:31.042
- I am not finished yet, captain!
- Oh, yes, you are, captain!

01:14:32.585 --> 01:14:33.745
Fräulein.

01:14:35.054 --> 01:14:39.184
Now, you will pack
your things this minute...

01:14:39.392 --> 01:14:41.883
...and return to the abbey.

01:14:44.530 --> 01:14:45.861
What's that?

01:14:47.600 --> 01:14:48.624
It's singing.

01:14:49.268 --> 01:14:52.066
Yes, I realize it's singing.
But who is singing?

01:14:53.039 --> 01:14:54.597
The children.

01:14:57.476 --> 01:14:58.807
The children?

01:14:59.378 --> 01:15:02.108
I taught them something to sing
for the baroness.

01:15:07.753 --> 01:15:13.783
<i>My heart wants to sing</i>
<i>Every song it hears</i>

01:15:14.060 --> 01:15:16.620
<i>Every song that it hears</i>

01:15:16.896 --> 01:15:22.334
<i>My heart wants to beat like the wings</i>
<i>Of the birds that rise</i>

01:15:22.601 --> 01:15:25.729
<i>From the lake to the trees</i>

01:15:25.971 --> 01:15:27.404
<i>To the trees</i>

01:15:27.640 --> 01:15:32.577
<i>My heart wants to sigh</i>
<i>Like a chime that flies</i>

01:15:32.778 --> 01:15:37.408
<i>From a church on a breeze</i>

01:15:37.683 --> 01:15:41.585
<i>To laugh like a brook</i>
<i>When it trips and falls</i>

01:15:41.854 --> 01:15:44.789
<i>Over stones on its way</i>

01:15:45.091 --> 01:15:46.456
<i>On its way</i>

01:15:46.692 --> 01:15:51.129
<i>To sing through the night</i>

01:15:51.330 --> 01:15:56.996
<i>Like a lark who is learning to pray</i>

01:15:57.269 --> 01:16:01.763
<i>I go to the hills</i>

01:16:01.974 --> 01:16:08.209
<i>When my heart is lonely</i>

01:16:08.481 --> 01:16:12.178
<i>I know I will hear</i>

01:16:12.451 --> 01:16:18.219
<i>What I've heard before</i>

01:16:19.058 --> 01:16:23.290
<i>My heart will be blessed</i>

01:16:23.529 --> 01:16:30.492
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:16:31.370 --> 01:16:36.569
<i>And I'll sing...</i>

01:16:36.809 --> 01:16:44.909
<i>...once more</i>

01:17:18.184 --> 01:17:19.947
Edelweiss!

01:17:23.923 --> 01:17:27.086
You never told me how enchanting
your children are.

01:17:35.701 --> 01:17:37.259
Don't go away.

01:17:42.374 --> 01:17:43.773
Fräulein.

01:17:47.112 --> 01:17:48.306
I...

01:17:49.782 --> 01:17:52.580
...behaved badly. I apologize.

01:17:54.320 --> 01:17:57.915
I'm far too outspoken.
It's one of my worst faults.

01:17:58.324 --> 01:17:59.791
You were right.

01:18:02.261 --> 01:18:04.161
I don't know my children.

01:18:05.464 --> 01:18:09.594
There's still time, captain.
They want so much to be close to you.

01:18:09.935 --> 01:18:13.803
And you brought music back
into the house.

01:18:15.140 --> 01:18:16.573
I'd forgotten.

01:18:19.311 --> 01:18:20.642
Fräulein.

01:18:23.148 --> 01:18:24.410
I want you to stay.

01:18:28.420 --> 01:18:31.150
I ask you to stay.

01:18:32.992 --> 01:18:36.484
- If I could be of any help.
- You have already.

01:18:37.096 --> 01:18:38.154
More than you know.

01:18:57.883 --> 01:18:59.214
Marta.

01:18:59.952 --> 01:19:01.180
Curtain!

01:19:03.856 --> 01:19:07.189
<i>High on a hill was a lonely goatherd</i>

01:19:08.694 --> 01:19:11.959
<i>Loud was the voice</i>
<i>Of the lonely goatherd</i>

01:19:13.465 --> 01:19:16.730
<i>Folks in a town</i>
<i>That was quite remote heard</i>

01:19:18.304 --> 01:19:21.535
<i>Lusty and clear</i>
<i>From the goatherd's throat heard</i>

01:19:33.052 --> 01:19:35.919
Marta. Marta!

01:19:38.324 --> 01:19:40.315
Gretl, the prince!

01:19:42.061 --> 01:19:45.519
<i>A prince on the bridge</i>
<i>Of a castle moat heard</i>

01:19:46.999 --> 01:19:49.331
<i>Men on a road</i>
<i>With a load to tote heard</i>

01:19:51.837 --> 01:19:55.102
<i>Men in the midst</i>
<i>Of a table d'hôte heard</i>

01:19:56.442 --> 01:19:59.707
<i>Men drinking beer</i>
<i>With the foam afloat heard</i>

01:20:10.789 --> 01:20:13.917
<i>One little girl</i>
<i>In a pale pink coat heard</i>

01:20:15.561 --> 01:20:18.894
<i>She yodeled back</i>
<i>To the lonely goatherd</i>

01:20:20.065 --> 01:20:23.466
<i>Soon her mama</i>
<i>With a gleaming gloat heard</i>

01:20:24.970 --> 01:20:28.269
<i>What a duet for a girl and goatherd</i>

01:21:14.853 --> 01:21:18.118
<i>One little girl</i>
<i>In a pale pink coat heard</i>

01:21:19.658 --> 01:21:22.923
<i>She yodeled back</i>
<i>To the lonely goatherd</i>

01:21:24.263 --> 01:21:27.699
<i>Soon her mama</i>
<i>With a gleaming gloat heard</i>

01:21:29.168 --> 01:21:32.296
<i>What a duet for a girl and goatherd</i>

01:21:34.006 --> 01:21:35.633
<i>Happy are they</i>

01:21:38.610 --> 01:21:41.875
<i>Soon the duet will become a trio</i>

01:22:06.371 --> 01:22:07.963
- Bravo!
- Bravo!

01:22:08.173 --> 01:22:09.663
Very good!

01:22:11.477 --> 01:22:13.377
Wonderful!

01:22:13.979 --> 01:22:17.142
- Can we keep the puppets, Uncle Max?
- Yes, can we?

01:22:17.349 --> 01:22:19.374
Of course you may, my darlings.

01:22:19.585 --> 01:22:23.817
Why else did I tell Professor Kohner
to send the bill to your father?

01:22:27.559 --> 01:22:29.220
Well done, fräulein.

01:22:31.730 --> 01:22:33.698
I really am very much impressed.

01:22:33.899 --> 01:22:35.890
They're your children, captain.

01:22:43.108 --> 01:22:45.406
My dear, is there anything
you can't do?

01:22:45.677 --> 01:22:48.009
Well, I'm not sure
I'll make a good nun.

01:22:48.247 --> 01:22:51.341
If you have any problems,
I'd be happy to help you.

01:22:54.453 --> 01:22:55.886
Attention, everyone!

01:22:56.088 --> 01:22:59.546
I have an announcement to make.
Surprise! Surprise!

01:22:59.791 --> 01:23:02.089
Today, after a long
and desperate search...

01:23:02.361 --> 01:23:07.355
...I have found a most exciting
entry for the Salzburg Folk Festival.

01:23:07.566 --> 01:23:09.397
Congratulations, Max.

01:23:09.635 --> 01:23:12.604
And who will you
be exploiting this time?

01:23:14.406 --> 01:23:17.603
- The Saint Ignatius Choir?
- Guess again.

01:23:18.310 --> 01:23:22.246
Well, let me see now.
The Klopmann Choir?

01:23:22.481 --> 01:23:24.881
- No, no, no, no.
- No, no?

01:23:25.083 --> 01:23:26.277
Tell us.

01:23:26.485 --> 01:23:29.943
A singing group all in one family.
You'll never guess, Georg.

01:23:30.222 --> 01:23:33.123
What a charming idea!

01:23:33.325 --> 01:23:35.122
Whose family?

01:23:35.994 --> 01:23:37.621
Yours.

01:23:37.829 --> 01:23:40.161
They'll be the talk of the festival.

01:23:43.001 --> 01:23:45.993
- Well, now, what's so funny?
- You are, Max.

01:23:46.271 --> 01:23:49.399
You're expensive, but very funny.

01:23:50.142 --> 01:23:52.474
- They'll be a sensation!
- No, Max.

01:23:52.744 --> 01:23:54.939
It's a wonderful idea.
Fresh, original.

01:23:55.147 --> 01:23:59.948
Max! My children
do not sing in public.

01:24:00.619 --> 01:24:02.587
You can't blame me for trying.

01:24:02.788 --> 01:24:05.780
Children, who shall we hear
from next?

01:24:08.594 --> 01:24:09.754
Who?

01:24:15.934 --> 01:24:17.128
Yes.

01:24:20.005 --> 01:24:21.939
The vote is unanimous.

01:24:22.774 --> 01:24:24.332
You, captain.

01:24:24.610 --> 01:24:25.804
Me?

01:24:26.645 --> 01:24:28.943
- I don't understand.
- Please.

01:24:35.153 --> 01:24:37.280
No, no, no, no.

01:24:37.556 --> 01:24:39.615
I'm told that you were quite good.

01:24:39.825 --> 01:24:43.124
- That was a very, very long time ago.
- I remember, Father.

01:24:43.362 --> 01:24:46.229
- Play us something we know.
- Oh, please, Father.

01:24:49.167 --> 01:24:50.225
Well...

01:25:00.479 --> 01:25:02.640
- Why didn't you tell me?
- What?

01:25:02.914 --> 01:25:05.212
To bring along my harmonica.

01:25:07.552 --> 01:25:09.679
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:11.256 --> 01:25:13.554
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:14.660 --> 01:25:20.860
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

01:25:21.099 --> 01:25:24.159
<i>Small and white</i>

01:25:25.003 --> 01:25:28.370
<i>Clean and bright</i>

01:25:28.573 --> 01:25:31.406
<i>You look happy...</i>

01:25:31.610 --> 01:25:35.444
<i>...to meet me</i>

01:25:35.714 --> 01:25:38.012
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

01:25:38.283 --> 01:25:42.413
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

01:25:42.621 --> 01:25:48.958
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

01:25:49.928 --> 01:25:53.625
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:53.865 --> 01:25:56.459
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:57.135 --> 01:26:04.405
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

01:26:08.780 --> 01:26:11.977
<i>- Edelweiss</i>
<i>- Edelweiss</i>

01:26:12.284 --> 01:26:15.776
<i>- Edelweiss</i>
<i>- Edelweiss</i>

01:26:15.987 --> 01:26:22.392
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

01:26:22.627 --> 01:26:26.154
<i>- Small and white</i>
<i>- Small and white</i>

01:26:26.431 --> 01:26:29.889
<i>- Clean and bright</i>
<i>- Clean and bright</i>

01:26:30.102 --> 01:26:32.593
<i>You look happy...</i>

01:26:32.838 --> 01:26:36.467
<i>...to meet me</i>

01:26:36.942 --> 01:26:39.069
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

01:26:39.277 --> 01:26:43.441
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

01:26:43.682 --> 01:26:50.747
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

01:26:50.989 --> 01:26:54.618
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:26:54.860 --> 01:26:57.522
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:26:58.130 --> 01:27:08.028
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

01:27:17.315 --> 01:27:20.978
Anytime you say the word, Georg,
you can be part of my new act:

01:27:21.186 --> 01:27:23.677
The von Trapp Family Singers.

01:27:24.790 --> 01:27:27.281
I have a wonderful idea, Georg.

01:27:27.526 --> 01:27:29.994
Let's really fill this house
with music.

01:27:30.228 --> 01:27:33.197
You must give a grand
and glorious party for me.

01:27:33.465 --> 01:27:36.161
- A party?
- Yes, Father, please!

01:27:36.368 --> 01:27:38.734
It's high time
I met all your friends...

01:27:39.037 --> 01:27:41.528
...and they met me.
Don't you agree?

01:27:41.807 --> 01:27:44.037
- I see what you mean.
- Oh, please!

01:27:44.309 --> 01:27:47.472
Children, it's bedtime.
Come now, say good night.

01:27:48.413 --> 01:27:49.710
Good night, Father.

01:27:49.915 --> 01:27:52.748
- Good night.
- Good night, Baroness Schraeder.

01:27:52.984 --> 01:27:54.542
Good night, Father.

01:27:57.522 --> 01:27:59.353
Good night, Uncle Max.

01:28:01.259 --> 01:28:04.422
It'll be my first party, Father!

01:28:36.962 --> 01:28:39.590
- Captain.
- Herr Zeller. Baroness Schraeder.

01:28:39.798 --> 01:28:42.926
- Good evening, Herr Zeller.
- Baroness.

01:28:44.236 --> 01:28:46.704
How do you do? Good evening.

01:29:07.325 --> 01:29:10.761
Did you notice the obvious
display of the Austrian flag?

01:29:17.836 --> 01:29:19.633
The women look so beautiful.

01:29:19.905 --> 01:29:21.236
I think they look ugly.

01:29:21.506 --> 01:29:23.337
You're just scared of them.

01:29:23.575 --> 01:29:25.805
Silly, only grown-up men fear women.

01:29:26.411 --> 01:29:29.972
- I think the men look beautiful.
- How would you know?

01:29:47.265 --> 01:29:49.290
Liesl, who are you dancing with?

01:29:49.501 --> 01:29:51.128
Nobody.

01:29:51.937 --> 01:29:53.837
Oh, yes, you are.

01:29:56.308 --> 01:29:57.798
May I have this dance?

01:29:58.009 --> 01:30:00.500
I'd be delighted, young man.

01:30:07.285 --> 01:30:09.947
Why didn't you tell me
you could dance?

01:30:10.188 --> 01:30:15.125
We feared you'd make us all dance.
The von Trapp Family Dancers.

01:30:19.531 --> 01:30:21.226
What are they playing?

01:30:21.466 --> 01:30:24.094
It's the Laendler.
An Austrian folk dance.

01:30:24.302 --> 01:30:27.465
- Show me.
- I haven't danced since I was little.

01:30:27.672 --> 01:30:29.640
You remember. Please?

01:30:29.908 --> 01:30:31.842
- Well...
- Please.

01:30:32.077 --> 01:30:34.307
All right. Come on over here.

01:30:34.813 --> 01:30:37.646
Now you bow and I curtsy.

01:30:38.583 --> 01:30:41.518
- Like this?
- Fine. Now we go for a little walk.

01:30:41.753 --> 01:30:44.415
One, two, three. One, two, three.

01:30:44.723 --> 01:30:49.319
One, two, three, step together.
Now, step hop, step hop.

01:30:49.561 --> 01:30:52.223
Now turn under. Not quite.

01:30:52.430 --> 01:30:56.389
This way. Hop step, hop.
And under.

01:30:57.068 --> 01:30:58.763
Kurt, we'll have to practice.

01:30:59.004 --> 01:31:00.494
Do allow me, will you?

01:32:28.793 --> 01:32:30.658
I don't remember anymore.

01:32:32.831 --> 01:32:35.026
- Your face is all red.
- Is it?

01:32:36.367 --> 01:32:38.460
I don't suppose I'm used to dancing.

01:32:41.172 --> 01:32:43.163
Why, that was beautifully done.

01:32:43.441 --> 01:32:45.341
What a lovely couple you make.

01:32:45.543 --> 01:32:47.670
It's time the children
said good night.

01:32:47.946 --> 01:32:49.277
We'll be in the hall.

01:32:49.514 --> 01:32:52.381
- We have something special prepared.
- Right!

01:32:52.684 --> 01:32:53.844
Yes, come on!

01:33:00.692 --> 01:33:03.024
All that needless worrying, Georg.

01:33:03.294 --> 01:33:06.320
You thought you wouldn't find
a friend at the party.

01:33:09.234 --> 01:33:12.829
- A bit chilly out tonight, isn't it?
- Oh, I don't know.

01:33:13.037 --> 01:33:15.062
It seemed rather warm to me.

01:33:19.244 --> 01:33:20.472
Ladies and gentlemen.

01:33:21.212 --> 01:33:25.308
The children of Captain von Trapp
wish to say good night to you.

01:33:39.430 --> 01:33:43.332
<i>There's a sad sort of clanging</i>
<i>From the clock in the hall</i>

01:33:43.535 --> 01:33:47.266
<i>And the bells in the steeple too</i>

01:33:47.539 --> 01:33:51.566
<i>And up in the nursery</i>
<i>An absurd little bird</i>

01:33:51.776 --> 01:33:54.210
<i>Is popping up to say "coo-coo"</i>

01:33:54.445 --> 01:33:56.106
<i>Coo-coo</i>

01:33:56.381 --> 01:33:57.609
<i>Coo-coo</i>

01:33:57.849 --> 01:34:00.010
<i>Regretfully they tell us</i>

01:34:00.218 --> 01:34:01.583
<i>But firmly they compel us</i>

01:34:01.853 --> 01:34:04.913
<i>To say goodbye</i>

01:34:05.123 --> 01:34:10.425
<i>To you</i>

01:34:13.631 --> 01:34:17.533
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, good night</i>

01:34:17.735 --> 01:34:21.603
<i>I hate to go</i>
<i>And leave this pretty sight</i>

01:34:28.880 --> 01:34:32.213
<i>So long, farewell,</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, adieu</i>

01:34:32.884 --> 01:34:36.411
<i>Adieu, adieu</i>
<i>To you and you and you</i>

01:34:43.761 --> 01:34:47.561
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Au revoir, auf Wiedersehen</i>

01:34:47.832 --> 01:34:51.768
<i>I'd like to stay</i>
<i>And taste my first champagne</i>

01:34:52.003 --> 01:34:54.437
- Yes?
- No.

01:34:58.776 --> 01:35:02.439
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

01:35:02.780 --> 01:35:06.739
<i>I leave and heave a sigh</i>
<i>And say goodbye</i>

01:35:06.951 --> 01:35:10.944
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:35:13.992 --> 01:35:17.086
<i>I'm glad to go</i>

01:35:17.328 --> 01:35:20.195
<i>I cannot tell a lie</i>

01:35:20.531 --> 01:35:23.523
<i>I flit, I float</i>

01:35:23.801 --> 01:35:27.259
<i>I fleetly flee, I fly</i>

01:35:37.315 --> 01:35:43.049
<i>The sun has gone to bed</i>

01:35:43.288 --> 01:35:47.019
<i>And so must I</i>

01:35:47.225 --> 01:35:49.625
<i>So long</i>

01:35:49.861 --> 01:35:52.421
<i>Farewell</i>

01:35:52.630 --> 01:35:58.034
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

01:35:58.303 --> 01:36:03.639
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:04.342 --> 01:36:09.905
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:10.148 --> 01:36:17.020
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:17.221 --> 01:36:25.720
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:30.735 --> 01:36:33.499
Extraordinary!
What they'd do at the festival.

01:36:33.738 --> 01:36:36.229
Young lady,
I must have a word with you.

01:36:37.241 --> 01:36:41.234
Georg, you won't let this girl
get away. She must join the party.

01:36:41.512 --> 01:36:43.912
- No, really l...
- Stop. Stop it now.

01:36:44.182 --> 01:36:47.117
- Georg, please.
- You can if you want to, fräulein.

01:36:47.352 --> 01:36:49.843
I insist.
You will be my dinner partner.

01:36:50.054 --> 01:36:51.954
This is business.
Franz...

01:36:52.223 --> 01:36:55.386
...set another place next to mine
for Fräulein Maria.

01:36:57.562 --> 01:37:00.292
- Whatever you say.
- It appears to be all arranged.

01:37:01.099 --> 01:37:02.964
- It does.
- I'm not suitably dressed.

01:37:04.035 --> 01:37:05.525
You can change. We'll wait.

01:37:09.140 --> 01:37:12.075
Captain, you must be very proud
of your youngsters.

01:37:12.276 --> 01:37:13.140
I am, thank you.

01:37:13.411 --> 01:37:17.973
Is there a more beautiful expression
of what is good in our country...

01:37:18.216 --> 01:37:21.652
...than the innocent voices
of our children?

01:37:22.053 --> 01:37:23.418
Oh, come now, baron.

01:37:23.654 --> 01:37:27.420
Would you have us believe that Austria
holds a monopoly on virtue?

01:37:28.326 --> 01:37:32.456
Herr Zeller, some of us prefer
Austrian voices raised in song...

01:37:32.663 --> 01:37:35.063
...to ugly German threats.

01:37:36.134 --> 01:37:39.763
The ostrich buries his head
in the sand...

01:37:39.971 --> 01:37:42.906
...and sometimes in the flag.

01:37:43.441 --> 01:37:47.639
Perhaps those who would warn you that
the Anschluss is coming, and it is...

01:37:47.912 --> 01:37:51.609
...would get further with you by setting
their words to music.

01:37:51.816 --> 01:37:56.480
If the Nazis take over Austria, you
will be the entire trumpet section.

01:37:56.788 --> 01:37:57.812
You flatter me.

01:37:58.856 --> 01:38:02.758
Oh, how clumsy of me.
I meant to accuse you.

01:38:10.501 --> 01:38:12.992
It's very kind of you
to offer to help me, baroness.

01:38:13.271 --> 01:38:14.829
I'm delighted, Maria.

01:38:15.306 --> 01:38:19.003
I really don't think I have anything
that would be appropriate.

01:38:19.477 --> 01:38:23.607
Now where is that lovely little thing
you were wearing the other evening?

01:38:23.848 --> 01:38:27.147
When the captain couldn't keep
his eyes off you.

01:38:30.521 --> 01:38:32.352
Couldn't keep his eyes off me?

01:38:33.691 --> 01:38:35.488
Come, my dear, we are women.

01:38:35.726 --> 01:38:39.127
Let's not pretend we don't know
when a man notices us.

01:38:39.363 --> 01:38:42.799
- Here we are.
- The captain notices everybody.

01:38:43.367 --> 01:38:45.801
There's no need to feel
so defensive, Maria.

01:38:46.037 --> 01:38:48.505
You are quite attractive, you know.

01:38:48.739 --> 01:38:52.368
The captain would hardly be a man
if he didn't notice you.

01:38:53.978 --> 01:38:56.344
Baroness, I hope you're joking.

01:38:56.814 --> 01:38:58.076
Not at all.

01:38:58.316 --> 01:38:59.908
I've never done a thing to...

01:39:00.184 --> 01:39:01.742
You don't have to, my dear.

01:39:02.386 --> 01:39:07.221
Nothing's more irresistible to a man
than a woman who's in love with him.

01:39:08.493 --> 01:39:10.927
- In love with him?
- Of course.

01:39:11.863 --> 01:39:15.264
What makes it so nice is
he thinks he's in love with you.

01:39:18.002 --> 01:39:19.594
But that's not true.

01:39:20.004 --> 01:39:23.496
Surely you've noticed the way
he looks into your eyes.

01:39:23.774 --> 01:39:28.677
And you know, you blushed in his arms
when you were dancing just now.

01:39:29.914 --> 01:39:31.609
Don't take it to heart.

01:39:31.883 --> 01:39:34.181
He'll get over it soon enough,
I think.

01:39:34.452 --> 01:39:36.420
Men do, you know.

01:39:37.421 --> 01:39:38.513
Then I should go.

01:39:39.857 --> 01:39:41.290
I mustn't stay here.

01:39:51.769 --> 01:39:55.205
- Is there something I can do to help?
- No, nothing.

01:39:56.974 --> 01:39:58.202
Yes.

01:39:59.210 --> 01:40:01.235
Don't say a word to the captain.

01:40:02.880 --> 01:40:06.441
No, I wouldn't dream of it.

01:40:13.224 --> 01:40:14.782
Goodbye, Maria.

01:40:15.593 --> 01:40:18.391
I'm sure you'll make a very fine nun.

01:40:48.426 --> 01:40:50.417
Champagne, darling.

01:40:50.828 --> 01:40:54.821
I feel like celebrating. Cheers.

01:41:00.304 --> 01:41:03.205
- You know something.
- Perhaps.

01:41:03.441 --> 01:41:07.969
If you're so clever, tell me how to
get fräulein to influence Georg.

01:41:08.212 --> 01:41:10.840
I want those children in the festival.

01:41:11.315 --> 01:41:13.613
Elsa, this is important to Austria.

01:41:13.818 --> 01:41:15.513
Wouldn't do you any harm either.

01:41:15.720 --> 01:41:17.312
I thought of that.

01:41:17.555 --> 01:41:20.023
Well, if it's a matter of influence...

01:41:20.224 --> 01:41:23.125
...maybe the one you have
to be talking to is me.

01:44:48.058 --> 01:44:50.288
- Two.
- Three.

01:44:50.560 --> 01:44:52.050
- Four.
- Five.

01:44:53.296 --> 01:44:55.321
- Six.
- Seven.

01:44:55.598 --> 01:44:57.225
Eight.

01:44:57.467 --> 01:44:59.298
- Four.
- Two.

01:45:00.403 --> 01:45:02.234
- Seven.
- Five.

01:45:02.472 --> 01:45:04.667
- Two.
- Six.

01:45:09.312 --> 01:45:11.337
Isn't this fun?

01:45:12.749 --> 01:45:15.081
- Four.
- I'm number five.

01:45:15.351 --> 01:45:17.512
- Oh, yes.
- Eight.

01:45:17.821 --> 01:45:20.187
- Two.
- Four.

01:45:20.590 --> 01:45:21.818
Six.

01:45:24.294 --> 01:45:25.522
Two.

01:45:26.663 --> 01:45:29.632
Baroness Schraeder, do you mind
if we stop now? We're tired.

01:45:29.866 --> 01:45:31.834
Whatever you want, dear.

01:45:32.102 --> 01:45:34.093
We'll do it again tomorrow.

01:45:44.280 --> 01:45:46.441
The country's so restful, isn't it?

01:45:47.484 --> 01:45:49.111
Have some lemonade.

01:45:50.353 --> 01:45:51.786
There must be an easier way.

01:45:53.189 --> 01:45:56.454
I get a fiendish delight thinking
of you as the mother of seven.

01:45:57.393 --> 01:45:59.224
How do you plan to do it?

01:45:59.496 --> 01:46:01.521
Darling, haven't you ever heard...

01:46:01.798 --> 01:46:04.892
...of a delightful little thing
called boarding school?

01:46:06.035 --> 01:46:08.299
Baroness Machiavelli.

01:46:09.639 --> 01:46:11.630
Uncle Max, where's Father?

01:46:11.908 --> 01:46:13.705
I think he's in the house.

01:46:13.910 --> 01:46:16.470
What's the matter
with all you gloomy pussies?

01:46:16.713 --> 01:46:19.511
- Nothing.
- I know. Let's have a rehearsal.

01:46:19.716 --> 01:46:20.614
What for?

01:46:20.817 --> 01:46:23.308
Let's make believe we're on-stage
at the festival.

01:46:23.520 --> 01:46:27.388
- I don't feel like singing.
- Not without Fräulein Maria.

01:46:27.657 --> 01:46:30.057
Liesl, get the guitar.
Come on, Marta.

01:46:30.260 --> 01:46:33.229
Everybody into the group.
Get in your places.

01:46:33.496 --> 01:46:36.260
Now be cheerful, right?
Give us the key, Liesl.

01:46:38.168 --> 01:46:40.830
Now, impress me.

01:46:44.841 --> 01:46:46.172
Gretl, why don't you sing?

01:46:46.442 --> 01:46:48.910
I can't. I've got a sore finger.

01:46:49.946 --> 01:46:53.006
But you sang so beautifully
the night of the party.

01:46:53.216 --> 01:46:55.548
Come on, all of you.
Try something you know.

01:46:55.785 --> 01:46:57.275
Enjoy it. Be cheerful.

01:46:57.554 --> 01:46:59.181
All right, Liesl.

01:47:01.124 --> 01:47:06.528
<i>The hills are alive</i>

01:47:06.763 --> 01:47:14.431
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:47:15.638 --> 01:47:20.701
<i>With songs they have sung</i>

01:47:20.944 --> 01:47:28.783
<i>For a thousand years</i>

01:47:29.485 --> 01:47:34.889
<i>The hills fill my heart</i>

01:47:35.124 --> 01:47:42.826
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:47:43.166 --> 01:47:45.794
They wanted to sing for me,
bless their hearts.

01:47:46.102 --> 01:47:48.002
That's lovely, lovely.
Don't stop.

01:47:52.008 --> 01:47:55.910
- Something long and cool, Georg?
- No, thank you, darling.

01:47:56.312 --> 01:47:58.746
- Father?
- Yes, Brigitta?

01:47:59.182 --> 01:48:01.446
Is it true Fräulein Maria
isn't coming back?

01:48:01.751 --> 01:48:04.845
Yes, I suppose it's true.
What have we got here?

01:48:05.154 --> 01:48:09.853
- Pink lemonade.
- Laced with lemonade.

01:48:10.593 --> 01:48:12.117
I don't believe it, Father.

01:48:13.496 --> 01:48:15.521
- What?
- About Fräulein Maria.

01:48:15.932 --> 01:48:17.160
Oh, Fräulein Maria!

01:48:17.467 --> 01:48:20.925
Didn't I tell you what her note said?
I'm sure I did.

01:48:21.671 --> 01:48:24.162
She said she missed her life
at the abbey.

01:48:24.440 --> 01:48:26.601
She had to leave us.

01:48:26.843 --> 01:48:28.435
And that's all there is to it.

01:48:30.146 --> 01:48:32.842
I think I'm brave enough to try
some of that.

01:48:33.049 --> 01:48:35.779
- She didn't even say goodbye.
- She did in her note.

01:48:36.052 --> 01:48:37.849
That isn't the same thing.

01:48:38.154 --> 01:48:39.781
Not too sweet, not too sour.

01:48:40.523 --> 01:48:42.514
Just too pink.

01:48:43.960 --> 01:48:47.054
Father, who is our new governess
going to be?

01:48:53.703 --> 01:48:54.795
Well...

01:48:57.140 --> 01:49:02.373
...you're not going to have
a governess anymore.

01:49:02.712 --> 01:49:05.374
- We're not?
- No.

01:49:07.583 --> 01:49:09.710
You're going to have a new mother.

01:49:10.820 --> 01:49:12.845
A new mother?

01:49:13.690 --> 01:49:16.818
We talked about it last night.
It's all settled.

01:49:17.026 --> 01:49:19.722
And we're all going to be very happy.

01:49:52.729 --> 01:49:55.197
Well, all right, all right.
Run off and play.

01:50:27.163 --> 01:50:28.130
Yes, my children?

01:50:28.331 --> 01:50:30.731
- My name is Liesl.
- Yes, Liesl?

01:50:31.234 --> 01:50:35.170
We, my brothers and sisters,
want to see Fräulein Maria.

01:50:36.339 --> 01:50:38.330
Fräulein Maria?

01:50:39.108 --> 01:50:41.076
Oh, Maria.

01:50:42.979 --> 01:50:44.810
Come in, please.

01:50:48.684 --> 01:50:50.242
Wait here.

01:51:01.197 --> 01:51:04.360
I'm Sister Margaretta. I understand
you inquired about Maria.

01:51:04.634 --> 01:51:07.125
We have to see her.
Will you tell her we're here?

01:51:07.370 --> 01:51:09.964
- I'm afraid I can't do that.
- But you've got to!

01:51:10.273 --> 01:51:12.332
- She's our governess.
- We want her back.

01:51:12.542 --> 01:51:14.442
She didn't even say goodbye.

01:51:14.677 --> 01:51:16.440
All we want to do is talk to her.

01:51:17.213 --> 01:51:20.114
I'm very sorry,
but Maria is in seclusion.

01:51:20.349 --> 01:51:23.443
- She hasn't been seeing anyone.
- She'll see us.

01:51:23.686 --> 01:51:26.177
I want to show her my finger.

01:51:26.389 --> 01:51:28.289
Some other time, dear.

01:51:28.558 --> 01:51:29.855
I'll tell her you were here.

01:51:30.126 --> 01:51:33.186
- It was sweet of you to call.
- We have to speak to her!

01:51:33.830 --> 01:51:36.958
Run along, children.
Run along home.

01:51:37.166 --> 01:51:38.793
I'm sure she'd like to see us.

01:51:39.068 --> 01:51:41.332
Sister Margaretta, please.

01:51:41.571 --> 01:51:45.302
- Goodbye, children.
- Sister Margaretta, may we, please?

01:51:48.077 --> 01:51:49.806
What was that about, Sister?

01:51:50.046 --> 01:51:52.241
The von Trapp children,
Reverend Mother.

01:51:52.482 --> 01:51:54.916
They want to see Maria.

01:51:55.184 --> 01:51:57.482
Has she spoken yet?
Has she told you anything?

01:51:57.753 --> 01:52:01.746
She doesn't say a word,
Reverend Mother, except in prayer.

01:52:02.024 --> 01:52:03.013
Poor child.

01:52:03.226 --> 01:52:06.195
It's strange.
She seems happy to be back here...

01:52:06.429 --> 01:52:09.728
...and yet she's unhappy too.

01:52:11.000 --> 01:52:14.060
Perhaps I have been wrong
in leaving her alone so long.

01:52:14.337 --> 01:52:17.033
Bring her to me,
even if she's not yet ready.

01:52:17.240 --> 01:52:18.901
Yes, Reverend Mother.

01:52:24.413 --> 01:52:27.905
Sister Augusta, take our new postulant
to the robing room.

01:52:28.918 --> 01:52:31.182
God bless you, my daughter.

01:52:37.393 --> 01:52:39.122
Yes, bring her in.

01:52:48.137 --> 01:52:50.401
You've been unhappy. I'm sorry.

01:52:52.441 --> 01:52:53.635
Reverend Mother.

01:52:53.976 --> 01:52:56.604
Why did they send you back to us?

01:52:57.446 --> 01:52:59.414
They didn't send me back.
I left.

01:53:01.918 --> 01:53:03.476
Sit down, Maria.

01:53:03.986 --> 01:53:05.783
Tell me what happened.

01:53:10.993 --> 01:53:12.324
I was frightened.

01:53:12.595 --> 01:53:17.055
- Frightened? Were they unkind to you.
- Oh, no!

01:53:17.300 --> 01:53:20.997
No, I was confused. I felt...

01:53:22.471 --> 01:53:24.564
I've never felt that way before.

01:53:24.807 --> 01:53:28.573
I couldn't stay. I knew that here
I'd be away from it. I'd be safe.

01:53:28.811 --> 01:53:33.510
Maria, our abbey is not to be used
as an escape.

01:53:33.783 --> 01:53:36.013
What is it you can't face?

01:53:37.987 --> 01:53:39.420
I can't face him again.

01:53:40.256 --> 01:53:41.780
Him?

01:53:43.359 --> 01:53:45.418
Thank you, Sister Margaretta.

01:53:55.037 --> 01:53:56.664
Captain von Trapp?

01:54:02.111 --> 01:54:04.807
- Are you in love with him?
- I don't know!

01:54:05.047 --> 01:54:06.514
I don't know. I...

01:54:07.049 --> 01:54:10.883
The baroness said I was.
She said that he was in love with me.

01:54:11.153 --> 01:54:13.815
But I didn't want to believe it.

01:54:14.890 --> 01:54:17.188
There were times we looked
at each other.

01:54:17.393 --> 01:54:18.951
I could hardly breathe.

01:54:19.328 --> 01:54:22.024
- Did you let him see your feelings?
- I don't know.

01:54:22.632 --> 01:54:25.294
That's what's torturing me.
I was on God's errand.

01:54:25.501 --> 01:54:30.495
To have asked for his love would have
been wrong. I just couldn't stay.

01:54:32.675 --> 01:54:35.473
I'm ready at this moment
to take my vows.

01:54:36.345 --> 01:54:39.405
- Please help me.
- Maria.

01:54:40.983 --> 01:54:45.682
The love of a man and a woman is holy.
You have a great capacity to love.

01:54:45.921 --> 01:54:48.856
You must find out how God
wants you to spend your love.

01:54:49.158 --> 01:54:52.992
But I pledged my life to God.
I pledged my life to his service.

01:54:53.195 --> 01:54:57.564
My daughter, if you love this man,
it doesn't mean you love God less.

01:54:59.235 --> 01:55:01.100
No.

01:55:01.337 --> 01:55:03.202
You must find out.

01:55:04.940 --> 01:55:07.431
You must go back.

01:55:07.710 --> 01:55:09.678
You can't ask me to do that.

01:55:09.879 --> 01:55:12.370
- Please let me stay. I beg...
- Maria.

01:55:12.581 --> 01:55:16.540
These walls were not built
to shut out problems.

01:55:16.752 --> 01:55:18.344
You have to face them.

01:55:18.921 --> 01:55:22.186
You have to live the life
you were born to live.

01:55:28.064 --> 01:55:32.364
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:55:32.601 --> 01:55:36.367
<i>Search high and low</i>

01:55:36.605 --> 01:55:41.372
<i>Follow every byway</i>

01:55:41.610 --> 01:55:45.876
<i>Every path you know</i>

01:55:46.315 --> 01:55:50.775
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:55:51.053 --> 01:55:55.387
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:55:55.624 --> 01:55:59.993
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:56:00.262 --> 01:56:04.596
<i>Till you find your dream</i>

01:56:04.800 --> 01:56:07.894
<i>A dream that will need</i>

01:56:08.137 --> 01:56:12.972
<i>All the love you can give</i>

01:56:13.743 --> 01:56:17.144
<i>Every day of your life</i>

01:56:17.413 --> 01:56:23.818
<i>For as long as you live</i>

01:56:24.120 --> 01:56:28.420
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:56:28.657 --> 01:56:32.991
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:56:33.262 --> 01:56:37.824
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:56:38.033 --> 01:56:46.441
<i>Till you find your dream</i>

01:56:47.543 --> 01:56:51.035
<i>A dream that will need</i>

01:56:51.347 --> 01:56:56.876
<i>All the love you can give</i>

01:56:57.153 --> 01:57:00.645
<i>Every day of your life</i>

01:57:00.890 --> 01:57:07.318
<i>For as long as you live</i>

01:57:07.563 --> 01:57:12.000
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:57:12.234 --> 01:57:16.170
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:57:16.839 --> 01:57:21.469
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:57:21.877 --> 01:57:25.973
<i>Till you find...</i>

01:57:26.215 --> 01:57:36.216
<i>...your dream</i>

01:57:38.761 --> 01:57:42.322
Now, it's not like my children
to be secretive.

01:57:42.565 --> 01:57:44.658
We're not being secretive, Father.

01:57:46.335 --> 01:57:49.668
And it's not like my children
to be late for dinner.

01:57:49.939 --> 01:57:53.375
- We lost track of the time.
- I see.

01:57:54.176 --> 01:57:57.577
Who's going to be the first one
to tell me the truth? Friedrich.

01:57:57.847 --> 01:57:59.906
Brigitta. Liesl.

01:58:01.283 --> 01:58:03.513
Where do you think we were, Father?

01:58:10.092 --> 01:58:14.051
If you don't believe us, you must have
some idea of where you think we were.

01:58:17.633 --> 01:58:19.430
- Marta.
- Yes, Father.

01:58:19.635 --> 01:58:20.897
You tell me.

01:58:22.238 --> 01:58:25.867
Friedrich told you, Father.
We were berry picking.

01:58:26.709 --> 01:58:31.373
- I forgot! You were berry picking.
- Yes, we love berry picking.

01:58:31.614 --> 01:58:32.706
All afternoon?

01:58:32.948 --> 01:58:34.677
- We picked thousands.
- Thousands?

01:58:34.884 --> 01:58:37.785
- They were all over the place.
- What kind of berries?

01:58:38.053 --> 01:58:41.318
- Blueberries, sir.
- Blueberries.

01:58:43.259 --> 01:58:46.626
It's too early for blueberries.

01:58:48.130 --> 01:58:50.223
- They were strawberries.
- Strawberries?

01:58:50.933 --> 01:58:53.629
It's been so cold lately,
they turned blue.

01:58:59.475 --> 01:59:01.636
Very well. Show me the berries.

01:59:02.912 --> 01:59:04.106
- We...
- Well...

01:59:04.346 --> 01:59:07.110
- Show me the berries you picked.
- We don't have them.

01:59:07.349 --> 01:59:09.613
You don't have them?
What happened to them?

01:59:09.852 --> 01:59:12.650
- We...
- We ate them.

01:59:12.855 --> 01:59:15.449
- You ate them?
- Yes!

01:59:15.658 --> 01:59:17.250
- They were so good.
- Delicious.

01:59:17.493 --> 01:59:18.687
Very well.

01:59:18.961 --> 01:59:24.092
Since you've obviously stuffed
yourselves on thousands of berries...

01:59:24.333 --> 01:59:28.269
...you can't be hungry anymore,
so I'll have to tell Frau Schmidt...

01:59:28.504 --> 01:59:31.371
...to skip your dinner.

01:59:40.549 --> 01:59:43.347
It's your fault.
We should have told him the truth.

01:59:43.619 --> 01:59:45.587
And made him boiling mad at us?

01:59:45.788 --> 01:59:47.722
It's better than starving to death.

01:59:47.957 --> 01:59:50.824
We didn't do anything wrong.
We just wanted to see her.

01:59:52.127 --> 01:59:55.221
My stomach's making noises.

01:59:55.664 --> 01:59:58.497
The least they could have done
was to let us say hello.

01:59:59.635 --> 02:00:03.537
- I wonder what grass tastes like.
- I feel awful.

02:00:03.973 --> 02:00:08.239
When Fräulein Maria wanted to feel
better she used to sing that song.

02:00:08.844 --> 02:00:10.311
Let's try it.

02:00:10.546 --> 02:00:13.208
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>

02:00:13.515 --> 02:00:17.542
<i>And whiskers on kittens</i>

02:00:18.387 --> 02:00:20.981
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>

02:00:21.190 --> 02:00:24.250
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

02:00:25.594 --> 02:00:31.555
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

02:00:31.834 --> 02:00:37.830
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

02:00:38.073 --> 02:00:40.098
Why don't I feel better?

02:00:41.276 --> 02:00:43.574
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>

02:00:43.846 --> 02:00:46.940
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

02:00:47.216 --> 02:00:52.848
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

02:00:53.222 --> 02:00:56.385
- <i>Silver white winters...</i>
- Fräulein Maria's back!

02:00:56.592 --> 02:00:57.889
<i>...that melt into springs</i>

02:00:58.293 --> 02:01:01.558
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

02:01:01.797 --> 02:01:04.891
<i>When the dog bites</i>
<i>When the bee stings</i>

02:01:05.100 --> 02:01:07.227
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

02:01:07.736 --> 02:01:10.705
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

02:01:10.973 --> 02:01:13.237
<i>And then I don't feel</i>

02:01:13.442 --> 02:01:20.211
<i>So bad</i>

02:01:20.449 --> 02:01:23.475
- Children, I'm so glad to see you.
- We missed you.

02:01:23.719 --> 02:01:24.708
I missed you.

02:01:24.987 --> 02:01:27.114
- Kurt, how are you?
- Hungry.

02:01:28.657 --> 02:01:31.285
- What happened to your finger?
- It got caught.

02:01:31.560 --> 02:01:33.721
- Caught in what?
- Friedrich's teeth.

02:01:34.963 --> 02:01:37.124
- Liesl, you all right?
- Just fair.

02:01:37.332 --> 02:01:40.324
- Any telegrams been delivered lately?
- None at all.

02:01:40.569 --> 02:01:44.005
But I'm learning to accept it.
I'll be glad when school begins.

02:01:44.306 --> 02:01:49.005
Liesl, you can't use school to escape
your problems. You have to face them.

02:01:49.244 --> 02:01:50.677
I have so much to tell you.

02:01:50.946 --> 02:01:52.937
We have things to tell you too.

02:01:53.282 --> 02:01:56.979
The most important thing is
that Father is going to be married.

02:01:57.186 --> 02:01:58.244
Married?

02:01:58.587 --> 02:02:00.612
Yes, to Baroness Schraeder.

02:02:08.530 --> 02:02:10.088
Oh, I see.

02:02:11.934 --> 02:02:15.301
Father, look!
Fräulein Maria's back!

02:02:15.537 --> 02:02:17.596
Fräulein Maria's back from the abbey.

02:02:19.808 --> 02:02:20.866
Good evening, captain.

02:02:22.344 --> 02:02:23.641
Good evening.

02:02:26.181 --> 02:02:28.012
Everyone inside for dinner.

02:02:28.317 --> 02:02:29.875
Dinner!

02:02:39.228 --> 02:02:43.961
You left without saying goodbye.
Even to the children.

02:02:44.967 --> 02:02:46.491
It was wrong of me. Forgive me.

02:02:48.537 --> 02:02:49.697
Why did you?

02:02:49.905 --> 02:02:52.738
Please don't ask me.
The reason no longer exists.

02:02:53.909 --> 02:02:57.003
Fräulein Maria, you've returned.

02:02:58.247 --> 02:03:00.044
Isn't it wonderful, Georg?

02:03:03.352 --> 02:03:05.582
I wish you every happiness,
baroness.

02:03:05.821 --> 02:03:08.517
You too, captain.
The children say you're to marry.

02:03:08.757 --> 02:03:09.883
Thank you, my dear.

02:03:12.427 --> 02:03:15.988
You are back to stay?

02:03:18.066 --> 02:03:21.399
Only until arrangements can be made
for another governess.

02:04:17.092 --> 02:04:18.719
There you are.

02:04:33.108 --> 02:04:35.576
I must speak to cook
about the schnitzel.

02:04:35.844 --> 02:04:39.143
It is entirely too delicious
for my figure.

02:04:39.581 --> 02:04:42.516
And it makes you much too quiet
at the dinner table.

02:04:42.784 --> 02:04:44.775
Or was it the wine?

02:04:45.020 --> 02:04:46.851
Undoubtedly the wine.

02:04:49.424 --> 02:04:51.688
You have no idea
the trouble I'm having...

02:04:51.960 --> 02:04:54.690
...trying to decide on
a wedding present for you.

02:04:54.997 --> 02:04:57.158
Oh, I know. I'm enough.

02:04:57.432 --> 02:05:01.027
But I do want you to have
some little trifle for the occasion.

02:05:01.270 --> 02:05:03.602
At first I thought
of a fountain pen...

02:05:03.839 --> 02:05:06.103
...but you've already got one.

02:05:06.375 --> 02:05:09.310
Then I thought perhaps a villa
in the south of France...

02:05:09.544 --> 02:05:12.206
...but they are so difficult
to gift-wrap.

02:05:12.481 --> 02:05:14.881
Oh, Georg, how do you
feel about yachts?

02:05:15.183 --> 02:05:17.447
A long, sleek one
for the Mediterranean...

02:05:17.686 --> 02:05:20.450
...or a tiny one
for your bathtub, huh?

02:05:22.624 --> 02:05:24.649
- Elsa.
- Where to go on our honeymoon?

02:05:24.893 --> 02:05:26.485
Now, that's a real problem.

02:05:26.695 --> 02:05:30.062
A trip around the world
would be lovely. And then I said:

02:05:30.365 --> 02:05:33.198
"Oh, Elsa, there must be
someplace better to go."

02:05:33.468 --> 02:05:35.902
- But don't worry, darling, I'll...
- Elsa.

02:05:36.571 --> 02:05:37.833
Yes, Georg.

02:05:38.840 --> 02:05:40.171
It's no use...

02:05:41.376 --> 02:05:42.741
...you and I.

02:05:44.313 --> 02:05:47.544
I'm being dishonest to both of us...

02:05:48.884 --> 02:05:50.545
...and utterly unfair to you.

02:05:55.824 --> 02:05:58.554
- When two people talk of marriage...
- No, don't.

02:05:59.428 --> 02:06:01.521
Don't say another word, please.

02:06:04.833 --> 02:06:09.861
You see, there are other things
I've been thinking of.

02:06:10.772 --> 02:06:15.505
Fond as I am of you, I really don't
think you're the right man for me.

02:06:18.046 --> 02:06:20.537
You're much too independent.

02:06:20.849 --> 02:06:25.548
And I need someone
who needs me desperately...

02:06:25.854 --> 02:06:28.846
...or at least needs
my money desperately.

02:06:31.026 --> 02:06:35.929
I've enjoyed every moment we've had
together and I do thank you for that.

02:06:38.700 --> 02:06:40.600
Now, if you'll forgive me...

02:06:40.802 --> 02:06:42.861
...I'll go inside,
pack my little bags...

02:06:43.105 --> 02:06:45.596
...and return to Vienna
where I belong.

02:06:50.979 --> 02:06:52.810
And somewhere out there...

02:06:53.115 --> 02:06:57.484
...is a young lady who, I think...

02:06:57.753 --> 02:06:58.981
...will never be a nun.

02:07:11.133 --> 02:07:13.465
Auf Wiedersehen, darling.

02:07:39.194 --> 02:07:40.354
Hello.

02:07:46.168 --> 02:07:49.763
I thought I just might find you here.

02:07:53.942 --> 02:07:56.206
Was there something you wanted?

02:07:56.645 --> 02:07:59.773
No, no, no. Sit down, please.

02:08:00.715 --> 02:08:02.046
Please.

02:08:07.189 --> 02:08:08.520
May I?

02:08:20.902 --> 02:08:25.635
You know, I was thinking
and I was wondering two things:

02:08:26.808 --> 02:08:31.040
Why did you run away to the abbey?

02:08:31.880 --> 02:08:36.544
And what was it
that made you come back?

02:08:38.220 --> 02:08:42.680
Well, I had an obligation
to fulfill...

02:08:42.891 --> 02:08:45.018
...and I came back to fulfill it.

02:08:45.660 --> 02:08:47.093
Is that all?

02:08:48.430 --> 02:08:50.591
And I missed the children.

02:08:50.932 --> 02:08:52.092
Yes.

02:08:53.368 --> 02:08:56.269
- Only the children?
- No. Yes.

02:08:56.505 --> 02:09:00.339
- Isn't it right that I missed them?
- Oh, yes. Yes, of course.

02:09:00.542 --> 02:09:03.170
I was only hoping that perhaps you...

02:09:04.279 --> 02:09:06.042
Perhaps you might...

02:09:07.782 --> 02:09:09.010
Yes?

02:09:10.785 --> 02:09:16.087
Well, nothing was the same
when you were away...

02:09:16.858 --> 02:09:20.089
...and it'll be all wrong again
after you leave...

02:09:20.295 --> 02:09:24.959
...and I just thought perhaps
you might change your mind.

02:09:29.037 --> 02:09:33.269
Well, I'm sure the baroness will be
able to make things fine for you.

02:09:33.542 --> 02:09:34.873
Maria...

02:09:36.978 --> 02:09:40.470
- There isn't going to be any baroness.
- There isn't?

02:09:42.884 --> 02:09:44.249
No.

02:09:44.553 --> 02:09:46.316
I don't understand.

02:09:48.723 --> 02:09:52.819
Well, we've called off our engagement,
you see, and...

02:09:53.094 --> 02:09:56.552
- Oh, I'm sorry.
- Yes. You are?

02:09:57.732 --> 02:09:59.825
- You did?
- Yes.

02:10:00.969 --> 02:10:05.497
Well, you can't marry someone
when you're...

02:10:08.076 --> 02:10:10.135
...in love with someone else...

02:10:13.515 --> 02:10:14.948
...can you?

02:10:49.818 --> 02:10:52.116
The Reverend Mother always says:

02:10:52.354 --> 02:10:55.790
"When the Lord closes a door,
somewhere He opens a window."

02:11:04.199 --> 02:11:07.225
What else does
the Reverend Mother say?

02:11:08.169 --> 02:11:10.569
That you have to look for your life.

02:11:12.240 --> 02:11:14.800
Is that why you came back?

02:11:18.847 --> 02:11:20.314
And have you found it...

02:11:21.316 --> 02:11:22.476
...Maria?

02:11:24.252 --> 02:11:26.243
I think I have.

02:11:28.990 --> 02:11:30.389
I know I have.

02:11:32.894 --> 02:11:34.555
I love you.

02:11:38.533 --> 02:11:40.398
Oh, can this be happening to me?

02:11:43.772 --> 02:11:49.176
<i>Perhaps I had a wicked childhood</i>

02:11:50.679 --> 02:11:55.912
<i>Perhaps I had a miserable youth</i>

02:11:57.786 --> 02:12:03.725
<i>But somewhere</i>
<i>In my wicked, miserable past</i>

02:12:04.225 --> 02:12:10.027
<i>There must have been a moment of truth</i>

02:12:10.965 --> 02:12:17.734
<i>For here you are</i>
<i>Standing there loving me</i>

02:12:18.473 --> 02:12:24.469
<i>Whether or not you should</i>

02:12:25.113 --> 02:12:31.916
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:12:32.787 --> 02:12:40.421
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:12:41.663 --> 02:12:44.632
<i>Nothing comes from nothing</i>

02:12:45.767 --> 02:12:49.635
<i>Nothing ever could</i>

02:12:50.472 --> 02:12:59.346
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:13:00.915 --> 02:13:10.415
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:13:11.292 --> 02:13:16.127
Do you know when I first
started loving you?

02:13:16.531 --> 02:13:20.433
That night at dinner, when you sat
on that ridiculous pine cone.

02:13:20.668 --> 02:13:21.965
What?

02:13:23.304 --> 02:13:26.762
I knew the first time you blew
that silly whistle.

02:13:27.675 --> 02:13:29.666
Oh, my love.

02:13:33.448 --> 02:13:41.355
<i>For here you are</i>
<i>Standing there loving me</i>

02:13:43.324 --> 02:13:49.160
<i>Whether or not you should</i>

02:13:50.532 --> 02:13:57.563
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:13:58.373 --> 02:14:06.075
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:14:07.248 --> 02:14:10.740
<i>Nothing comes from nothing</i>

02:14:11.486 --> 02:14:14.512
<i>Nothing ever could</i>

02:14:14.756 --> 02:14:20.558
<i>So somewhere in my youth...</i>

02:14:20.829 --> 02:14:23.059
<i>...or childhood</i>

02:14:26.167 --> 02:14:32.697
<i>I must have done something</i>

02:14:34.742 --> 02:14:47.382
<i>Something good</i>

02:14:54.095 --> 02:14:55.619
Maria.

02:14:57.465 --> 02:15:02.061
Is there anyone I should go to,
to ask permission to marry you?

02:15:05.974 --> 02:15:08.534
- Why don't we ask...
- The children?

02:16:57.051 --> 02:17:01.078
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

02:17:01.889 --> 02:17:05.586
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

02:17:06.561 --> 02:17:10.725
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

02:17:11.165 --> 02:17:12.154
<i>A flibbertigibbet</i>

02:17:12.400 --> 02:17:15.665
<i>A will-o'-the-wisp</i>
<i>A clown</i>

02:17:15.870 --> 02:17:20.432
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

02:17:20.875 --> 02:17:24.902
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

02:17:25.613 --> 02:17:29.913
<i>But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>And listen to all you say?</i>

02:17:30.284 --> 02:17:34.220
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

02:17:34.555 --> 02:17:39.549
<i>Oh, how do you solve</i>
<i>A problem like Maria?</i>

02:17:39.927 --> 02:17:46.560
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam</i>
<i>In your hand?</i>

02:19:52.660 --> 02:19:54.218
Herr Detweiler!

02:19:56.831 --> 02:19:59.493
- Heil Hitler.
- Oh, good afternoon, Herr Zeller.

02:19:59.734 --> 02:20:03.033
Perhaps you've not heard.
I am now the Gauleiter.

02:20:03.337 --> 02:20:04.861
Heil Hitler.

02:20:05.773 --> 02:20:06.933
Heil Hitler.

02:20:07.241 --> 02:20:09.505
I've come from
Captain von Trapp's house.

02:20:09.944 --> 02:20:13.539
The only one in the area
not flying the Third Reich flag...

02:20:13.781 --> 02:20:15.043
...since the Anschluss.

02:20:15.249 --> 02:20:17.410
- But we have dealt with that.
- I don't...

02:20:17.685 --> 02:20:20.620
The housekeeper told me
that I would find you here.

02:20:20.888 --> 02:20:22.583
The only thing she'd tell me.

02:20:23.090 --> 02:20:25.615
What kind of information
are you looking for?

02:20:25.893 --> 02:20:27.758
When will the captain return?

02:20:28.296 --> 02:20:32.232
Well, he's on his honeymoon trip.
He's not been in touch with us.

02:20:32.466 --> 02:20:37.301
Am I to believe he hasn't communicated
with his children in over a month?

02:20:37.572 --> 02:20:39.472
How many men do you know...

02:20:39.740 --> 02:20:43.039
...who communicate with their children
while honeymooning?

02:20:43.945 --> 02:20:47.642
Upon his return, he'll fill
his proper position in the new order.

02:20:47.949 --> 02:20:50.315
Naturally.
And may I congratulate you...

02:20:50.551 --> 02:20:55.215
...and your people in allowing the
festival to go on tonight as planned.

02:20:55.756 --> 02:20:59.214
Why should it not go on?
Nothing in Austria has changed.

02:20:59.460 --> 02:21:02.861
Singing and music will
show this to the world.

02:21:03.064 --> 02:21:04.759
Austria is the same.

02:21:05.633 --> 02:21:06.998
Heil Hitler.

02:21:09.170 --> 02:21:10.762
Heil Hitler.

02:21:12.440 --> 02:21:13.668
Come, let's go home.

02:21:13.908 --> 02:21:17.400
- Why was he so cross?
- Everybody's cross these days.

02:21:17.612 --> 02:21:20.979
Maybe the flag with the black spider
makes people nervous.

02:21:21.182 --> 02:21:24.117
- Will Father be in trouble?
- He doesn't have to be.

02:21:24.352 --> 02:21:27.082
The thing to do
is to get along with everybody.

02:21:27.321 --> 02:21:29.516
Remember that tonight at the concert.

02:21:29.757 --> 02:21:32.658
Are we really going to sing
before a lot of people?

02:21:32.860 --> 02:21:34.953
Look. The von Trapp Family Singers:

02:21:35.162 --> 02:21:39.758
Liesl, Friedrich, Louisa, Brigitta,
Kurt, Marta and Gretl.

02:21:39.967 --> 02:21:44.336
- Why am I always last?
- Because you are the most important.

02:21:45.039 --> 02:21:46.666
There we go.

02:21:52.546 --> 02:21:56.004
Are you sure Father will approve
of our singing in public?

02:21:56.217 --> 02:21:58.515
He'll be pleased and proud.

02:21:58.986 --> 02:22:01.454
- Liesl, do you think so?
- Don't you trust me?

02:22:01.656 --> 02:22:02.680
No.

02:22:02.890 --> 02:22:04.983
You're a very intelligent girl.

02:22:05.526 --> 02:22:07.687
Liesl. Liesl!

02:22:08.629 --> 02:22:09.823
Rolfe!

02:22:10.831 --> 02:22:12.856
I'm so glad to see you.
It's been su...

02:22:13.067 --> 02:22:14.159
Good afternoon.

02:22:14.568 --> 02:22:17.503
Give this to your father
as soon as he's home.

02:22:18.172 --> 02:22:20.037
- He's on his honeymoon.
- I know.

02:22:20.241 --> 02:22:23.574
- You do?
- We make it our business to know all.

02:22:24.312 --> 02:22:26.872
- Who's "we"?
- See that he gets it.

02:22:27.081 --> 02:22:29.413
- What is it?
- It's a telegram from Berlin.

02:22:30.251 --> 02:22:32.742
Don't you want to deliver it yourself?

02:22:33.220 --> 02:22:35.848
I'm occupied
with more important matters.

02:22:36.057 --> 02:22:38.548
And your father had better be too.

02:22:38.826 --> 02:22:40.316
But, Rolfe!

02:23:03.417 --> 02:23:05.078
Father!

02:23:05.353 --> 02:23:08.015
- We didn't expect you so soon.
- Hello, hello!

02:23:08.255 --> 02:23:11.053
We didn't expect you home
until next week!

02:23:11.258 --> 02:23:16.696
- Did you bring souvenirs from Paris?
- Hello! How are you?

02:23:17.798 --> 02:23:19.095
Why didn't you call us?

02:23:19.300 --> 02:23:21.234
We couldn't get through.

02:23:21.535 --> 02:23:23.469
I had nothing to do with that.

02:23:23.738 --> 02:23:25.763
We came back as fast as we could.

02:23:26.073 --> 02:23:28.234
Well, well, well! We missed you!

02:23:28.476 --> 02:23:30.910
- We missed you!
- We missed kissing you.

02:23:31.112 --> 02:23:33.945
We missed all the noise
in the morning.

02:23:34.215 --> 02:23:38.413
- Mostly, we missed hearing you sing.
- Oh, you came back just in time.

02:23:38.619 --> 02:23:40.382
Look, Fräulein Maria...

02:23:40.588 --> 02:23:42.215
I mean Mother.

02:23:42.623 --> 02:23:45.114
We're going to sing
in the festival tonight.

02:23:45.326 --> 02:23:47.453
We've been having a lovely time!

02:23:47.728 --> 02:23:49.787
We've been rehearsing all...

02:23:51.298 --> 02:23:53.630
Surprise! Surprise!

02:23:54.301 --> 02:23:56.792
Surprises for you on the terrace.

02:23:59.840 --> 02:24:01.239
We'll talk about this.

02:24:01.442 --> 02:24:05.742
I would've told you but you were away.
I had to make a last-minute decision.

02:24:06.013 --> 02:24:08.504
I was fortunate to enter them at all.

02:24:08.749 --> 02:24:13.482
They'll be the talk of the festival.
Imagine, seven children in one family!

02:24:13.687 --> 02:24:15.314
Max!

02:24:15.923 --> 02:24:18.756
Somehow I recall having made it
quite clear to you...

02:24:19.026 --> 02:24:21.688
...how I feel about my family
singing in public!

02:24:21.962 --> 02:24:23.657
The committee was enchanted.

02:24:23.864 --> 02:24:27.027
- What did they say?
- I have never heard such enthusiasm.

02:24:27.301 --> 02:24:31.601
- Don't you think just this once...?
- Absolutely out of the question.

02:24:31.839 --> 02:24:35.969
- Georg, this is for Austria.
- For Austria?

02:24:36.343 --> 02:24:39.608
- There is no Austria!
- But the Anschluss was peaceful.

02:24:39.847 --> 02:24:43.305
- Let's at least be grateful for that.
- Grateful?

02:24:45.186 --> 02:24:46.847
You know, Max...

02:24:47.721 --> 02:24:50.986
...sometimes I don't believe
I know you.

02:24:53.661 --> 02:24:55.026
Father, I forgot.

02:24:55.863 --> 02:24:57.455
This is for you.

02:25:07.241 --> 02:25:11.234
Maria, he has got to at least pretend
to work with these people.

02:25:11.512 --> 02:25:13.036
You must convince him.

02:25:13.247 --> 02:25:16.011
Max, I can't ask him
to be less than he is.

02:25:16.250 --> 02:25:19.549
Then I'll talk to him.
If the children don't sing, well...

02:25:19.820 --> 02:25:22.050
...it will be a reflection
on Austria.

02:25:22.857 --> 02:25:26.224
Oh, I know.
It wouldn't do me any good either.

02:25:31.398 --> 02:25:34.060
Mother? That sounds so nice.

02:25:34.335 --> 02:25:37.065
- I like calling you "Mother."
- I like hearing it.

02:25:37.271 --> 02:25:41.002
You love Father very much.
I can tell you do.

02:25:41.208 --> 02:25:42.004
Very much.

02:25:42.276 --> 02:25:45.575
Mother, what do you do when you
think you love someone?

02:25:46.280 --> 02:25:51.582
I mean, when you stop loving someone
or he stops loving you?

02:25:54.188 --> 02:25:56.247
Well, you cry a little.

02:25:56.690 --> 02:25:58.783
Then you wait for the sun to come out.

02:25:59.093 --> 02:26:00.424
It always does.

02:26:00.694 --> 02:26:04.255
There are so many things I think
I should know but I don't.

02:26:04.465 --> 02:26:06.433
- I really don't.
- How can you?

02:26:06.700 --> 02:26:08.895
Sometimes I feel the world is ending.

02:26:09.136 --> 02:26:12.367
- Then you feel it's just beginning?
- Yes!

02:26:12.573 --> 02:26:16.805
It was that way with me. And for you
it will be just as wonderful.

02:26:17.478 --> 02:26:19.378
Do you really think so?

02:26:20.281 --> 02:26:24.217
<i>When you're 16 going on 17</i>

02:26:24.485 --> 02:26:28.080
<i>Waiting for life to start</i>

02:26:28.756 --> 02:26:32.590
<i>Somebody kind</i>
<i>Who touches your mind</i>

02:26:32.826 --> 02:26:37.126
<i>Will suddenly touch your heart</i>

02:26:37.565 --> 02:26:39.260
<i>When that happens</i>

02:26:39.733 --> 02:26:41.667
<i>After it happens</i>

02:26:41.902 --> 02:26:45.770
<i>Nothing is quite the same</i>

02:26:46.006 --> 02:26:47.564
<i>Somehow I know</i>

02:26:47.841 --> 02:26:49.968
<i>I'll jump up and go</i>

02:26:50.177 --> 02:26:54.477
<i>If ever he calls my name</i>

02:26:54.748 --> 02:26:58.650
<i>Gone are your old ideas of life</i>

02:26:58.919 --> 02:27:03.117
<i>The old ideas grow dim</i>

02:27:03.357 --> 02:27:07.760
<i>Lo and behold</i>
<i>You're someone's wife</i>

02:27:08.696 --> 02:27:14.692
<i>And you belong to him</i>

02:27:15.002 --> 02:27:19.302
<i>You may think this kind of adventure</i>

02:27:19.506 --> 02:27:23.374
<i>Never may come to you</i>

02:27:24.478 --> 02:27:29.848
<i>Darling, 16 going on 17</i>

02:27:30.684 --> 02:27:34.814
<i>Wait a year...</i>

02:27:35.623 --> 02:27:40.856
<i>- I'll wait a year</i>
<i>...or two</i>

02:27:41.295 --> 02:27:48.633
<i>Just wait a year...</i>

02:27:49.503 --> 02:27:58.138
<i>...or two</i>

02:28:00.547 --> 02:28:02.139
Liesl.

02:28:18.599 --> 02:28:19.930
What is it?

02:28:20.868 --> 02:28:22.233
Berlin.

02:28:22.703 --> 02:28:24.568
They've offered me a commission.

02:28:24.838 --> 02:28:27.363
I've been requested
to accept immediately...

02:28:27.608 --> 02:28:31.601
...and report to their naval base
at Bremerhaven tomorrow.

02:28:32.212 --> 02:28:36.205
I knew this would happen.
I didn't think it would be so soon.

02:28:36.450 --> 02:28:39.942
To refuse them would be fatal
for all of us.

02:28:41.188 --> 02:28:44.954
And joining them would be unthinkable.

02:28:51.131 --> 02:28:52.894
Get the children all together.

02:28:53.233 --> 02:28:56.430
Don't say anything to worry them.
Just get them ready.

02:28:57.404 --> 02:28:59.770
We've got to get out of Austria...

02:29:01.442 --> 02:29:03.103
...and this house...

02:29:05.446 --> 02:29:06.879
...tonight.

02:29:50.791 --> 02:29:53.191
This strains my back
and breaks my heart...

02:29:53.460 --> 02:29:56.293
...when I think of the children
missing the festival.

02:29:56.597 --> 02:29:59.259
By your announcement
we'll be over the border.

02:29:59.500 --> 02:30:01.934
Do you appreciate
the sacrifice I'm making?

02:30:02.136 --> 02:30:03.433
You have no choice.

02:30:03.670 --> 02:30:06.503
I know. That's why I'm making it.

02:30:07.207 --> 02:30:09.334
Why doesn't Father turn the motor on?

02:30:09.543 --> 02:30:12.979
Because he doesn't want anyone
to hear us.

02:30:16.617 --> 02:30:19.051
What will Frau Schmidt and Franz say?

02:30:19.319 --> 02:30:22.846
They'll be able to answer honestly
they didn't know anything.

02:30:23.056 --> 02:30:27.288
- Will we be coming back here?
- Someday, Liesl. I do hope someday.

02:30:27.528 --> 02:30:32.465
Are Father and Uncle Max going to push
the car all the way to Switzerland?

02:30:59.259 --> 02:31:01.659
Something wrong
with your car, captain?

02:31:01.995 --> 02:31:04.259
Yes, we couldn't get it started.

02:31:08.035 --> 02:31:09.263
Karl.

02:31:11.238 --> 02:31:14.730
Fix Captain von Trapp's car
so that it will start.

02:31:37.931 --> 02:31:39.728
Excellent, Karl.

02:31:43.103 --> 02:31:46.266
I've not asked you where you
and your family are going.

02:31:46.773 --> 02:31:48.900
Nor have you asked me why I'm here.

02:31:49.109 --> 02:31:52.875
Apparently we both suffer
from a deplorable lack of curiosity.

02:31:53.747 --> 02:31:56.215
You never answered the telegram...

02:31:56.450 --> 02:31:59.749
...from the Admiral of the Navy
of the Third Reich.

02:31:59.987 --> 02:32:02.455
I was under the impression,
Herr Zeller...

02:32:02.723 --> 02:32:06.215
...that the contents of telegrams
in Austria are private!

02:32:06.927 --> 02:32:10.454
At least, the Austria I know.

02:32:11.598 --> 02:32:13.225
I have my orders...

02:32:13.467 --> 02:32:15.628
...to take you
to Bremerhaven tonight...

02:32:15.903 --> 02:32:18.098
...where you will accept
your commission.

02:32:19.239 --> 02:32:24.677
I'm afraid that's going to be
quite impossible.

02:32:25.279 --> 02:32:27.008
You see, we...

02:32:27.581 --> 02:32:30.414
...all of us, the entire family,
will be...

02:32:31.485 --> 02:32:33.510
...singing in the festival tonight.

02:32:33.820 --> 02:32:36.288
As a matter of fact, we're going now.

02:32:36.924 --> 02:32:39.791
We couldn't possibly
let them down now.

02:32:39.993 --> 02:32:42.962
- I just hope we're not too late.
- Yes.

02:32:43.196 --> 02:32:46.097
You ask me to believe that you,
Captain von Trapp...

02:32:46.333 --> 02:32:47.800
...are singing in a concert?

02:32:48.201 --> 02:32:52.331
Believe me, it will be a performance
beyond anything even I've dreamt of.

02:32:52.706 --> 02:32:57.336
Like you, Herr Zeller,
I, too, am a man of hidden talents.

02:32:58.045 --> 02:32:59.376
Yes.

02:32:59.646 --> 02:33:02.137
Here, program.

02:33:07.154 --> 02:33:09.486
It says only the names
of the children.

02:33:09.723 --> 02:33:12.988
It says
the von Trapp Family Singers...

02:33:13.226 --> 02:33:16.286
...and I am the head of
the von Trapp family, am I not?

02:33:18.565 --> 02:33:22.365
And these travel clothes
that you're all wearing?

02:33:23.203 --> 02:33:24.727
Our costumes, naturally.

02:33:25.005 --> 02:33:28.406
This night air is not good
for the children's voices.

02:33:34.648 --> 02:33:38.175
Well, a slight delay in my orders
will not be serious.

02:33:39.386 --> 02:33:40.910
Therefore...

02:33:41.755 --> 02:33:43.382
...you will sing.

02:33:44.324 --> 02:33:46.315
You will all sing.

02:33:46.693 --> 02:33:49.218
But only because that's what I want.

02:33:50.163 --> 02:33:53.599
It will demonstrate that nothing
in Austria has changed.

02:33:54.334 --> 02:33:56.529
And when you have finished singing...

02:33:56.837 --> 02:34:00.000
...you, Captain von Trapp, will be
taken to Bremerhaven.

02:34:01.274 --> 02:34:04.004
Now, if you will all get
into your car...

02:34:04.244 --> 02:34:08.078
...we will escort the von Trapp Family
Singers to the festival.

02:34:08.949 --> 02:34:11.110
No escort will be necessary.

02:34:11.351 --> 02:34:13.842
Necessary? A pleasure, captain.

02:34:14.755 --> 02:34:18.623
After all, we would not want you
to get lost in the crowds.

02:34:19.860 --> 02:34:21.350
Would we?

02:34:22.029 --> 02:34:23.189
No.

02:34:39.413 --> 02:34:42.576
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

02:34:42.783 --> 02:34:45.980
<i>La, a note to follow sew</i>

02:34:46.253 --> 02:34:49.711
<i>Tea, a drink with jam and bread</i>

02:34:49.923 --> 02:34:53.723
<i>A drink with jam and bread</i>

02:35:03.303 --> 02:35:05.464
<i>Tea with jam</i>
<i>Jam and bread</i>

02:35:11.344 --> 02:35:14.677
<i>- With jam</i>
<i>- A, B, C</i>

02:35:14.915 --> 02:35:18.146
<i>- With jam</i>
<i>- Do-re-mi</i>

02:35:18.351 --> 02:35:21.946
<i>Tea with jam and bread</i>

02:35:22.189 --> 02:35:23.520
<i>With jam and bread</i>

02:35:23.790 --> 02:35:25.314
<i>With jam</i>
<i>With jam...</i>

02:35:25.525 --> 02:35:34.331
<i>...and bread</i>

02:35:56.323 --> 02:35:59.451
My fellow Austrians...

02:36:00.727 --> 02:36:05.289
...I shall not be seeing you again,
perhaps for a very long time.

02:36:06.700 --> 02:36:08.361
I would like to sing for you now...

02:36:09.970 --> 02:36:11.528
...a love song.

02:36:13.507 --> 02:36:15.702
I know you share this love.

02:36:17.010 --> 02:36:20.707
I pray that you will never let it die.

02:36:33.493 --> 02:36:37.020
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:36:37.230 --> 02:36:40.427
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:36:40.700 --> 02:36:46.434
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

02:36:46.840 --> 02:36:49.900
<i>Small and white</i>

02:36:50.177 --> 02:36:52.941
<i>Clean and bright</i>

02:36:53.513 --> 02:36:58.610
<i>You look happy to meet me</i>

02:36:59.386 --> 02:37:01.411
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

02:37:01.688 --> 02:37:05.283
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

02:37:05.525 --> 02:37:11.191
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

02:37:12.699 --> 02:37:15.190
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:15.435 --> 02:37:18.063
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:18.271 --> 02:37:24.267
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

02:37:28.782 --> 02:37:31.876
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:32.118 --> 02:37:33.449
<i>Edel...</i>

02:37:40.827 --> 02:37:43.921
<i>Small and white</i>

02:37:44.130 --> 02:37:46.997
<i>Clean and bright</i>

02:37:47.234 --> 02:37:52.570
<i>You look happy to meet me</i>

02:37:53.406 --> 02:37:55.374
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

02:37:55.575 --> 02:37:58.976
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

02:37:59.646 --> 02:38:05.642
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

02:38:06.119 --> 02:38:09.020
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:38:09.322 --> 02:38:12.086
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:38:12.692 --> 02:38:20.929
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

02:38:38.652 --> 02:38:40.210
I think it'll work.

02:38:40.954 --> 02:38:42.717
I shall miss all of you.

02:38:43.223 --> 02:38:45.657
I shall miss the money
I could have made with you.

02:38:49.062 --> 02:38:50.620
Thank you, ladies and gentlemen.

02:38:51.364 --> 02:38:54.026
The competition has come
to its conclusion...

02:38:54.301 --> 02:38:57.395
...except, we don't know
yet what that conclusion will be.

02:38:58.371 --> 02:39:00.896
And while the judges
arrive at their decision...

02:39:01.174 --> 02:39:04.200
...I have been given permission
to offer you an encore.

02:39:04.477 --> 02:39:07.674
This will be the last opportunity
the von Trapps will have...

02:39:07.914 --> 02:39:10.314
...of singing together
for a long, long time.

02:39:11.384 --> 02:39:15.377
Even now, officials are waiting
in this auditorium...

02:39:15.655 --> 02:39:18.385
...to escort Captain von Trapp
to his new command...

02:39:18.591 --> 02:39:22.152
...in the naval forces
of the Third Reich.

02:39:26.833 --> 02:39:31.361
And so, ladies and gentlemen,
the family von Trapp again...

02:39:32.005 --> 02:39:34.269
...to bid you farewell.

02:39:41.514 --> 02:39:45.109
<i>There's a sad sort of clanging</i>
<i>From the clock in the hall</i>

02:39:45.385 --> 02:39:48.718
<i>And the bells in the steeple too</i>

02:39:49.222 --> 02:39:53.090
<i>And up in the nursery</i>
<i>An absurd little bird</i>

02:39:53.293 --> 02:39:55.727
<i>Is popping out to say "coo-coo"</i>

02:39:55.929 --> 02:39:57.590
<i>Coo-coo</i>

02:39:57.864 --> 02:39:58.853
<i>Coo-coo</i>

02:39:59.132 --> 02:40:00.724
<i>Regretfully they tell us</i>

02:40:00.934 --> 02:40:02.731
<i>But firmly they compel us</i>

02:40:02.969 --> 02:40:05.733
<i>To say goodbye</i>

02:40:05.939 --> 02:40:11.104
<i>To you</i>

02:40:14.080 --> 02:40:17.607
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, good night</i>

02:40:17.884 --> 02:40:21.615
<i>We hate to go</i>
<i>And miss this pretty sight</i>

02:40:27.794 --> 02:40:31.389
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, adieu</i>

02:40:31.598 --> 02:40:35.261
<i>Adieu, adieu</i>
<i>To you and you and you</i>

02:40:41.574 --> 02:40:45.169
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

02:40:45.412 --> 02:40:47.004
<i>We flit, we float</i>

02:40:47.280 --> 02:40:48.941
<i>We fleetly flee, we fly</i>

02:40:55.321 --> 02:40:59.121
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

02:40:59.325 --> 02:41:02.692
<i>The sun has gone to bed</i>
<i>And so must I</i>

02:41:02.962 --> 02:41:06.762
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:07.000 --> 02:41:12.700
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:12.939 --> 02:41:18.138
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:18.378 --> 02:41:25.546
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:57.350 --> 02:42:01.480
Ladies and gentlemen, I have here the
decision of our distinguished judges.

02:42:01.688 --> 02:42:04.248
We will start with the award
for third prize.

02:42:04.891 --> 02:42:07.223
For this honor,
the judges have named...

02:42:07.494 --> 02:42:12.090
...the first soloist of the choir
of St. Agatha's Church in Murback.

02:42:12.365 --> 02:42:14.595
Fräulein Schweiger.

02:42:51.538 --> 02:42:55.474
Second prize
to The Toby Reiser Quintet.

02:43:23.436 --> 02:43:27.600
And the first prize,
the highest honor in all Austria...

02:43:27.840 --> 02:43:30.934
...the von Trapp Family Singers.

02:43:43.323 --> 02:43:44.984
The family von Trapp.

02:43:59.606 --> 02:44:00.664
They're gone!

02:44:19.359 --> 02:44:20.792
Come with me.

02:44:24.631 --> 02:44:26.622
Quickly, quickly.

02:44:27.533 --> 02:44:29.728
I have a place you can hide.

02:44:30.470 --> 02:44:33.735
Slowly, slowly.

02:44:44.717 --> 02:44:46.412
Open this gate.

02:44:47.553 --> 02:44:49.145
Good evening.

02:44:51.658 --> 02:44:53.091
Hurry up, woman.

02:45:12.945 --> 02:45:14.207
Two men in there.

02:45:14.414 --> 02:45:16.279
Six of you cover the yard.

02:45:16.516 --> 02:45:18.746
You two, cover the corridor.

02:45:33.232 --> 02:45:36.793
Reverend Mother, we didn't realize
we put the abbey in this danger.

02:45:37.070 --> 02:45:39.595
No, Maria, it was right for you
to come here.

02:45:39.806 --> 02:45:41.706
We thought we might borrow
your car.

02:45:41.908 --> 02:45:43.808
I'm afraid our car will do you
no good now.

02:45:44.410 --> 02:45:46.071
I've been listening to the wires.

02:45:46.279 --> 02:45:48.804
The borders have just been closed.

02:45:54.654 --> 02:45:56.952
All right,
if the borders are closed...

02:45:58.257 --> 02:46:01.556
...then we'll drive up into the hills
and go over the mountains on foot.

02:46:02.161 --> 02:46:04.152
- The children...
- We'll help them.

02:46:04.430 --> 02:46:06.591
We can do it without help, Father.

02:46:07.633 --> 02:46:08.998
Maria.

02:46:09.736 --> 02:46:12.330
You will not be alone.
Remember:

02:46:12.572 --> 02:46:15.666
"I will lift up mine eyes unto
the hills from whence cometh my help."

02:46:16.642 --> 02:46:17.734
Yes, Mother.

02:46:19.112 --> 02:46:21.273
- I'm scared.
- Me too.

02:46:33.359 --> 02:46:34.519
God be with you.

02:46:41.467 --> 02:46:43.025
- Mother.
- Yes?

02:46:43.269 --> 02:46:46.466
Would it help if we sang
about our favorite things?

02:46:46.706 --> 02:46:49.698
No, darling.
This is one time it would not help.

02:46:49.976 --> 02:46:53.173
You must be very quiet.
Hold tight to me.

02:49:07.847 --> 02:49:09.075
Let's try the roof.

02:50:05.338 --> 02:50:07.568
Rolfe, please.

02:50:12.678 --> 02:50:14.168
No, wait.

02:50:23.990 --> 02:50:25.321
Maria.

02:50:26.392 --> 02:50:27.825
Children.

02:50:31.864 --> 02:50:34.890
It's you we want, not them.

02:50:35.267 --> 02:50:36.996
Put that down.

02:50:38.070 --> 02:50:41.369
Not another move,
or I'll shoot.

02:50:43.075 --> 02:50:45.100
You're only a boy.

02:50:48.114 --> 02:50:51.777
- You don't really belong to them.
- Stay where you are.

02:50:53.552 --> 02:50:55.543
Come away with us.

02:50:56.789 --> 02:50:57.949
Before it's too late.

02:50:58.557 --> 02:51:00.889
Not another step.
I'll kill you.

02:51:03.195 --> 02:51:06.528
- You give that to me, Rolfe.
- Did you hear me?

02:51:07.533 --> 02:51:09.091
I'll kill you.

02:51:10.970 --> 02:51:12.437
Rolfe.

02:51:30.823 --> 02:51:32.154
You'll never be one of them.

02:51:34.927 --> 02:51:36.622
Lieutenant!

02:51:36.896 --> 02:51:38.022
They're here!

02:51:38.230 --> 02:51:39.788
They're here, lieutenant!

02:52:21.107 --> 02:52:22.768
Reverend Mother.

02:52:24.043 --> 02:52:25.874
I have sinned.

02:52:27.046 --> 02:52:29.207
I too, Reverend Mother.

02:52:30.850 --> 02:52:33.182
What is this sin, my children?

